    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Assistant-Lecturer-Assistant-Teaching-Professor-of-Entrepreneurship_R-03020-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Lecturer/Assistant Teaching Professor of Entrepreneurship",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-25\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Lecturer/Assistant Teaching Professor of Entrepreneurship Compensation: $60,000 - $90,000 Department: Management Start Date: 01/01/2027 About this opportunity: The Department of Management in the Miller College of Business at Ball State University welcomes applications for a full-time, 10-month contract position with a joining date of January 2027 or August 2027, based on the availability of the candidate and needs of the department. This contract position is renewable based upon the performance of the employee, teaching needs of the department, and budget. Candidates should have the ability to be physically present on Ball State campus multiple days per week and should be prepared to teach both face-to-face and online courses. Student needs will determine the final count of in-person vs online courses. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the United States without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you will bring: Position Function: Primary responsibilities include teaching courses in the field of entrepreneurship and/or other areas of management (e.g., leadership, human resource management, international business, organizational behavior). Duties and Responsibilities: Teaching: Anticipated assignments include teaching four classes (12 credits) per semester in the field of entrepreneurship and/or other areas of management (e.g., leadership, human resource management, international business, organizational behavior). Service: Performing service and outreach activities for Ball State University and the community. Minimum Qualifications: Master’s degree in business or related field from an accredited institution. Previous teaching experience at the undergraduate collegiate level.     Preferred Qualifications: Master’s or doctoral degree in business or related field from an AACSB-accredited institution. Significant teaching experience in entrepreneurship at an AACSB-accredited institution. Proven record of service and outreach in the field of entrepreneurship. Required Certifications/Licensures: How to apply: For inquiries about this position, please contact: Dr. Abhishek Srivastava, abhishek.srivastava@bsu.edu Please follow upload instructions and attach all required supporting application documents listed below. Only applications submitted through Workday, which include all required documents listed below, will be considered. Required Application Documents: Curriculum Vitae *Please do not use the Autofill feature for resume/vitae Letter of application Teaching Statement When prompted, please provide name and contact information for (3) references within the application Optional Documents: Transcripts may be uploaded at the time of application, however, an official transcript must be received by the issuing institution at the time of employment. Application Deadline: This position will remain open until filled with the consideration date of September 30, 2026. Candidates submitting application materials on or before this date will receive full consideration. Review of applications will continue until the position is filled. What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer 12 paid sick days and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Faculty and download our calculator spreadsheet."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Assistant-Professor-of-Marketing_R-02895-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Marketing",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-25\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Professor of Marketing Compensation: $132,000-$137,000 Department: Marketing Start Date: 08/01/2027 About this opportunity: The Department of Marketing in the Miller College of Business at Ball State University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Marketing position beginning August 2027. We are a collaborative, student-centered, industry-connected, experientially driven, and forward-looking department committed to preparing students for successful careers in a rapidly changing marketing profession. The successful candidate will join the department at an exciting point in its development. We are strengthening our curriculum, expanding applied learning and industry engagement, and creating more intentional connections across the student experience. The candidate will contribute their own expertise and ideas while working with others to help shape what comes next. We value faculty interested in connecting classroom learning with meaningful applied and immersive experiences that help students develop the knowledge, skills, judgment, and professional readiness needed to succeed. We are seeking a candidate who is excited to contribute through excellent teaching, meaningful scholarship, collaborative engagement, and a genuine investment in the continued growth of our students, programs, and department. The ideal candidate will demonstrate a strong commitment to helping students navigate emerging developments in marketing, including evolving technologies, digital platforms, data-informed decision making, and other innovations shaping the profession. Candidates with an interest and ability to teach undergraduate and/or graduate marketing courses, particularly in one or more of the following areas are strongly encouraged to apply: digital marketing, marketing research, consumer behavior, and marketing analytics. Employer will consider sponsorship. What you'll do and what you will bring: Position Function Primary responsibilities include teaching undergraduate and/or graduate marketing courses, maintaining an active program of scholarly research, and contributing to the continued success of the Department of Marketing through meaningful service, student engagement, and collaboration with colleagues. Duties and Responsibilities Teaching: Teach 9 semester credit hours of undergraduate and/or graduate marketing courses, with assignments based on departmental needs and the faculty member's expertise. Deliver high-quality instruction in face-to-face and online environments. Develop engaging learning experiences that connect theory and practice through applied, immersive, and industry-engaged learning opportunities, when appropriate. Research: Maintain an active and productive program of scholarly research that demonstrates the potential for sustained scholarly achievement consistent with departmental, college, and AACSB expectations for tenure and promotion. Disseminate research through quality peer-reviewed publications, academic conferences, and other appropriate scholarly outlets. Contribute to a collaborative research culture through scholarly engagement, interdisciplinary collaboration, and when appropriate, the involvement and mentorship of students in research activities. Service: Contribute meaningful service to the department, college, university, profession, and broader community. Contribute to departmental initiatives that advance student success, curriculum innovation, industry engagement, and the department’s shared priorities. Collaborate with colleagues, students, alumni, and external partners to strengthen the department and enhance the student experience. Minimum Qualifications Education: Ph.D. or D.B.A. in Marketing or a closely related field from an AACSB-accredited institution. Candidates with ABD will be considered and must demonstrate satisfactory progress toward completion of the doctoral degree consistent with university policy. Experience: Evidence of, or demonstrated potential for, high-quality scholarly research. Evidence of, or demonstrated potential for, effective university-level teaching. Preferred Qualifications Evidence of effective university teaching. Teaching interests or expertise in one or more of the following areas: digital marketing, marketing research, consumer behavior, or marketing analytics. Evidence of an active research pipeline and potential for sustained scholarly productivity. Interest or experience in applied and immersive learning. Demonstrated ability to collaborate effectively with colleagues and contribute to a collegial, student-centered department. How to apply: For inquiries about this opportunity, please contact: Department Chair, Jamye Foster ( jamye.foster@bsu.edu ) Please follow upload instructions to attach all of the required supporting application documents listed below. Only complete applications submitted through Workday will be considered. REQUIRED APPLICATION DOCUMENTS: A cover letter addressing qualifications and interest in the position A current résumé or curriculum vitae - Please do not use the Autofill feature for resume Academic philosophy highlighting how your candidacy aligns with Ball State University's values Within the application, please provide contact information for three professional references The option to upload your transcript is available but is not required at the time of application. Original, official transcripts from the issuing institution reflecting the highest related earned degree is required at the time of hire (even if your degree is obtained at Ball State University). This position will remain open until filled with the consideration date: September 27, 2026. Candidates submitting application materials on or before this date will receive full consideration. Review of applications will continue until position is filled. What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer 12 paid sick days and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Faculty and download our calculator spreadsheet."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Assistant-Professor-of-Leadership-Organizational-Behavior_R-02774": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Leadership/Organizational Behavior",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-10\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Professor of Leadership/Organizational Behavior Compensation: $130,000 - $133,000 Department: Management Start Date: 08/01/2027 About this opportunity: The Department of Management in the Miller College of Business at Ball State University welcomes applications for a full-time, tenure-track faculty member at the rank of Assistant Professor with expertise in Leadership, Organizational Behavior, or related fields. Tenure status is not granted automatically; it is awarded based on demonstrated excellence in performance, budgetary considerations, tenure density, and the needs of the university. The university will consider sponsorship. What you'll do and what you will bring: Position Function: Primary responsibilities include teaching undergraduate and graduate courses, conducting scholarly research in the areas of leadership, organizational behavior, or related fields, and service to the university and profession. Duties and Responsibilities: Teaching: Teach up to 9 semester hours of undergraduate and/or graduate courses, both on-campus and online. Teaching reduction is available for exceptional research performance. Time release and summer stipend is available for recent PhD. graduates. Research: Conduct scholarly research, primarily in the area of leadership, organizational behavior, or related fields, and publish in high-quality academic journals. Service: Actively contribute in service roles to Ball State University, local community, and the academic profession.   Minimum Qualifications: Education: PhD from an AACSB-accredited institution in management or a closely related field with emphasis on leadership or organizational behavior topics. ABD candidates will be considered during the selection process. Experience: Evidence of scholarly research and teaching experience in business-related field. Teaching: At least one semester of higher education teaching experience in the field of management at an AACSB-accredited institution.   Preferred Qualifications: Teaching: At least one-year (9 months) of teaching experience in leadership, organizational behavior, or human resource management at an AACSB-accredited institution with preference for candidates that have interest and ability in teaching organizational change. Research: A record of publications in prestigious refereed journals in management. Service: Contributions to a prominent organization that serves academic professionals.   Required Certifications/Licensures: How to apply: For inquiries about this opportunity, please contact: Dr. Abhishek Srivastava (abhishek.srivastava@bsu.edu) I mportant: Please follow upload instructions for attaching all required documents listed below . Only complete applications will be considered.  REQUIRED APPLICATION DOCUMENTS: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae - *Please do not use the Autofill feature for your resume/vitae Statement of teaching philosophy Statement of research agenda References - Within the application, you will be prompted to provide names and contact information for three (3) professional references. NOTE: Reference checks will not be conducted until the final round of the candidate selection process. This position will remain open until filled with a consideration date of September 15, 2026. Candidates submitting application materials on or before this date will receive full consideration. Review of applications will continue until the position is filled.  What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer 12 paid sick days and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Faculty and download our calculator spreadsheet."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Instructor-of-English-as-Another-Language_R-02795": {
      "title": "Instructor of English as Another Language",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-07\nPart time\n\nPosition Title:   Instructor of English as Another Language Compensation: $1,600.00 - $2,000.00 Department: Div of Lifetime Learning, NonCredit - Temp Start Date: 08/31/2026 About this opportunity:   We are seeking qualified, enthusiastic, and culturally competent candidates to join our Part-Time Adjunct Instructor Pool for Adult EAL (English as Another Language).  We offer 8-week cohorts throughout the year, with our next session starting at the end of August. Applicants admitted to this pool will be reviewed and hired on an as-needed basis prior to the start of each cohort. Our in-person classes are taught at different locations: Fishers, Indianapolis, and Whitestown. We are currently seeking faculty for the Fishers location.  This is a part-time temporary position teaching 32 hours total (2 hours, twice a week in the evenings) for 8 weeks. Continued teaching opportunities may be available. Salary will be based on experience. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring:   Position Description: In this role, instructors facilitate dynamic, practical language instruction for adult learners aiming to improve their English for personal, professional, or academic goals. Position function and duties: Instruction:  Deliver engaging, learner-centered English lessons focusing on speaking, listening, reading, and writing for real-world adult contexts.  Lesson Preparation:  Plan and adapt curriculum to meet the diverse needs, skill levels, and cultural backgrounds of adult students.  Classroom Management:  Foster a safe, supportive, and inclusive learning environment where adult students feel confident practicing new skills.  Assessment & Tracking:  Monitor student progress, provide constructive feedback, and maintain accurate attendance records.  Communication:  Coordinate with program administrators regarding curriculum, student needs, and facility logistics. Minimum qualifications  Education:  Bachelor’s degree preferably in education, English, or TESOL  Experience:  Prior teaching experience  Skills:  Strong cross-cultural communication and interpersonal skills.  Flexibility, patience, and enthusiasm for working with adult learners.  Reliable transportation to your assigned location (Fishers, Indianapolis, or Whitestown). How to apply:   Submit your cover letter and cv. IMPORTANT: To ensure accurate processing of your application, do not rely on a resume upload to populate the job experience section. All work history must be entered directly into the application fields. If questions please contact Nell Hill at nrhill@bsu.edu"
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Assistant-Professor-of-Forensic-Science_R-02661": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Forensic Science",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-05\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Professor of Forensic Science Compensation: $65,000 - $75,000 Department: Criminal Justice & Criminology Start Date: 08/16/2027 About this opportunity: The College of Sciences and Humanities at Ball State University invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the Assistant Professor level in forensic science. Preference will be given to individuals with practical experience in forensic science. The successful applicant will be housed in a department commiserate with the candidate’s expertise. A Ph.D. in forensic science, biology, chemistry, or forensic psychology or a closely related ﬁeld is required at the time of appointment. Employer will consider sponsorship. What you'll do and what you will bring: Duties and Responsibilities: Teaching responsibilities comprise introductory and advanced courses in forensic science and/or courses in content areas that contribute to the forensic science program. Other teaching could include undergraduate and/or graduate courses in the home department. Applicants are expected to possess a strong commitment to excellence in teaching at the undergraduate level and provide leadership in further forensic science program development. The selected candidate will also be expected to develop and maintain an independent and active research program, mentor student researchers, and provide service to the profession, university, and program. Minimum Qualifications: An earned Doctorate degree appropriate for a forensic science program, preferably in biology, chemistry, or a related ﬁeld by time of appointment. Research experience in a forensic science discipline or in methods and techniques adapted, supported, and employed by the forensic science community. Excellent written and oral communication skills. Preferred Qualifications: The ability to establish effective collaborative relationships with a varied range of internal and external populations . Record of successful teaching in a college/university environment . Established scholarship record in forensic science, biology, chemistry, or forensic psychology . How to apply: For inquiries, please contact: Dr. Benjamin Gibbs - Search Committee Chair brgibbs@bsu.edu,  765-285-5102 Please follow upload instructions to attach all of the required supporting documents listed below: NOTE: Do not use the Autofill feature for resume: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Consideration Date: to ensure full consideration, applications must be received by October 1st, 2026. (Applications will continue to be accepted after the full consideration date, until a sufficient applicant pool has been achieved or the position is filled. The closing date is subject to change without notice to applicants.) What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer 12 paid sick days and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Faculty and download our calculator spreadsheet."
