    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Instructors-of-Nutrition-and-Health-Science_R-02778": {
      "title": "Instructors of Nutrition and Health Science",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-22\nPart time\n\nPosition Title:   Instructors of Nutrition and Health Science Compensation: $3000-$9000 Department: Dept of Nutrition & Health Science - Temp Start Date: 08/17/2026 About this opportunity:   The Department of Nutrition and Health Science invites applications for part-time faculty semester appointments to teach classes in public health, research methods, or nutrition/dietetics; face-to-face on the Ball State campus in Muncie, Indiana OR online. Original official transcripts and licensure/credentials in respective field of expertise are required at time of hire. The applicant pool will be used for up to one year from the posting date to hire individuals. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring:   Position Function : Teach face-to-face courses on the main campus in Muncie, Indiana, or online courses. Minimum Qualifications: For public health: Master’s degree or higher in public health, epidemiology, biostatistics, public health informatics, or related ﬁeld from an accredited institution by date of appointment Minimum of 1 year of successful on-campus university teaching experience or related work experience For research methods courses, professional experience in research is also needed, such as work for a research study in a funded research grant For nutrition/dietetics: Master’s degree or higher in nutrition or closely related field from an accredited institution by date of appointment Minimum of 1 year of successful on-campus university teaching experience or related work experience For research methods courses, professional experience in research is also needed, such as work for a research study in a funded research grant For medical nutrition therapy courses, RDN required Preferred Qualifications: Additional years of successful college or university teaching experience and/or work experience, including research experience. How to apply:   For inquiries, please contact : Dr. Alyce Fly, Chairperson – adfly@bsu.edu , 765-285-1502 Please follow upload instructions to attach all of the required supporting documents listed below: NOTE: Do not use the Autofill feature for resume. 1. Cover Letter 2. Curriculum Vitae In support of your application for this position, please prepare and submit a cover letter that describes how your qualifications and experience align with the elements of the position description (or leadership profile)."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Temporary-Burris-Athletic-Coach_R-02749-1": {
      "title": "Temporary Burris Athletic Coach",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-20\nPart time\n\nPosition Title:   Temporary Burris Athletic Coach Compensation: $500-$6,0000, based on coaching role Department: Burris Laboratory School - Temp A Start Date: 07/20/2026 About this opportunity:   Burris Laboratory School is seeking part-time, temporary athletic coaches to support and mentor students on various teams. Hours will include evenings and some weekends. Compensation is determined by specific role and responsibilities and normal range is $500.00-$6000.00 for the season. Candidates for this position must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring:   Position function : Provide coaching and training to student athletes. ​ Duties/Responsibilities: Coaching and Training: Develop and implement training programs Student Development : Help students establish personal and team goals. Game Management : Plan game strategies, select players Safety and Compliance: Ensure a safe environment for athletes, adhere to all school and safety standards, complete required safety training and implement necessary. Promote sportsmanship among athletes. Administrative Tasks: record keeping and reporting to school administrators and athletic director. Minimum Education and Experience : High school diploma or equivalent Knowledge of applicable sport Must be able to effectively communicate to students, parents, officials, school administration. How to apply:   For Inquiries, please contact: Athletic Director, Mack Rathbun: mack.rathbun@bsu.edu Required Documents:   Resume   Cover letter-optional but preferred   Three references should be provided     IMPORTANT: To ensure accurate processing of your application, do not rely on a resume upload to populate the job experience section. All work history must be entered directly into the application fields.      Requires successful completion of a background check and education verification."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Instructor-of-Nursing_R-02689": {
      "title": "Instructor of Nursing",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-16\nPart time\n\nPosition Title:   Instructor of Nursing Compensation: $3,000 to $12,000 Department: School of Nursing - Temp Start Date: 08/17/2026 About this opportunity:   The School of Nursing welcomes applications from Master’s or Doctoral-prepared nurse educators with clinical experience for part-time, adjunct faculty positions for the baccalaureate program. Work assignments, days, times, and locations vary. The School has clinical instructional opportunities for well-qualified nurse educators Tues. through Sun. - morning, afternoon, and evening - in our expanding undergraduate program. Candidates must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. Please note, if you apply for this position, you may not hear from the department until there is a need to hire an instructor. What you'll do and what you'll bring:   Position Description: Part-time, contract faculty member with appropriate nursing specialization to teach in undergraduate courses. Work assignments, days, times, and locations vary. Faculty responsibilities include teaching in classroom, clinical, and/or simulation environments in baccalaureate courses for adult health, medical-surgical, psychiatric mental health, pediatrics, critical care, childbearing families, and other courses as appropriate. Duties and Responsibilities: Teach in classroom, clinical, and/or simulation environments in baccalaureate courses. Keep abreast of recent developments in nursing and incorporate into teaching. Actively contribute to the professional life of the School of Nursing, the College of Health, and Ball State University. Minimum Qualifications: Master's degree in nursing from an accredited college or university by the date of appointment; AND Clinical nursing experience in area of teaching; AND Ability to communicate effectively Preferred Qualifications: Teaching experience in higher education; Earned doctorate in nursing or related field from an accredited college or university. Required Certifications/Licensures: Current unencumbered State of Indiana Registered Nurse License by date of appointment. How to apply:   Please follow upload instructions to attach all of the required supporting documents listed below: IMPORTANT: To ensure accurate processing of your application, do not rely on a resume upload to populate the job experience section. All work history must be entered directly into the application fields. REQUIRED: Curriculum Vitae or Resume Contact information for 3 references Cover Letter - In your cover letter, please include the following information: • Your interest in teaching in-person, online, or both; Specific days and times, including weekends and evenings if applicable, you would be available to teach an in-person clinical section. RN licensure documentation Please bundle your documents into one document to ensure that you can include all required items. OPTIONAL: Transcripts (will be required upon hire) NP Certification Please note that RN licensure documentation must contain applicant’s name, license number, and current license expiration date, and be a copy, scan, or screenshot from an authoritative source. Questions about the opportunity can be directed to nursing@bsu.edu."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Assistant-Teaching-Professor_R-02633": {
      "title": "Assistant Teaching Professor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-14\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Teaching Professor Compensation: $45,000 - $55,000 Department: History Start Date: 01/01/2027 About this opportunity: The Department of History at Ball State University offers undergraduate students’ courses to fulfill their course of study for their major, minor, or core curriculum. The position of oral historian will teach classes to gather information from informants through immersive learning projects. The results of these projects will be collected and stored in the university library and shared through community partners Full time - 40 hrs. per week Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you will bring: Duties and Responsibilities: Using the master syllabus create a course syllabus and Canvas page, create in person instruction, perform assessment including midterms and finals, record and maintain documents. Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. or ABD in history or related field by date of appointment. Experience with oral history in modern world history, and commitment to immersive learning instructional practices (see website). Preferred Qualifications: Experience teaching HIST 152 Modern world history   How to apply: For inquiries, please contact: Ronald Morris at rvmorris@bsu.edu Please follow upload instructions to attach all of the required supporting documents listed below: NOTE: Do not use the Autofill feature for resume: Curriculum Vitae Teaching evaluations if available Consideration Date: to ensure full consideration, applications must be received by October 5th, 2026. (Applications will continue to be accepted after the full consideration date, until a sufficient applicant pool has been achieved or the position is filled. The closing date is subject to change without notice to applicants.) What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer 12 paid sick days and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Faculty and download our calculator spreadsheet."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Assistant-Professor-of-History_R-01745": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of History",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-04-29\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Professor of History Compensation: $62,000 - $70,000 Department: History Start Date: 08/16/2027 About this opportunity: The Department of History has a tenure-track position in Social Studies Education available August 2027. Ball State Social Studies Education students are highly desired as classroom teachers. Employer will consider sponsorship. What you'll do and what you will bring: Duties and Responsibilities: Primary responsibilities include teaching undergraduate and graduate courses in social studies methodologies, supervising student teachers, writing accreditation reports and supervising a degree option within the history department that involves interaction with other departments and programs and serves over 100 of our majors. Candidate must also have an active research agenda leading to product in the form of presentations, publications and the like.   Minimum Qualifications: ABD in social studies education or related field; Ph. D. or Ed.D. in social studies education or related field expected from an accredited college or university by August 2, 2027; must have active research agenda and record of effective teaching, including 24 months of experience teaching social studies at the middle or secondary school level.   Preferred Qualifications: Ph.D. or Ed.D. in social studies education or related field; teaching experience at the college or university level; interest in using digital approaches that help distill historical meaning from texts and artifacts and present historical analysis in a classroom setting; interest in civic engagement; and record of scholarship, including publication and/or presentation in primary area(s) of scholarship; record of service in relevant social studies/history and related associations; experience supervising student teachers; license to teach social studies or history at the secondary level; record of building successful partnerships with K-12 schools.   Required Certifications: Must be able to meet the minimum standards for Indiana State teaching license. How to apply: For inquiries, please contact: Ronald Morris at 765-285-8720 or rvmorris@bsu.edu . Please follow upload instructions to attach all of the required supporting documents listed below: NOTE: Do not use the Autofill feature for resume: Cover Letter Vitae 3 years of teaching evaluations Samples of publications Consideration Date: to ensure full consideration, applications must be received by October 1st, 2026. (Applications will continue to be accepted after the full consideration date, until a sufficient applicant pool has been achieved or the position is filled. The closing date is subject to change without notice to applicants.) What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer 12 paid sick days and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Faculty and download our calculator spreadsheet."
