    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Assistant-Associate-Professor-and-Program-Director-of-Counseling-Psychology_R-01020-1": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor and Program Director of Counseling Psychology",
      "description": "Posted: 2025-10-30\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant/Associate Professor and Program Director of Counseling Psychology Compensation: 65,000-75,000 Department: Counsel Psych, Social Psych & Couns Start Date: 08/21/2026 About this opportunity: The Department of Counseling Psychology, Social Psychology, and Counseling invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor who will serve as the next Program Director of Counseling Psychology for our APA accredited PhD program. Employer will consider sponsorship. What you'll do and what you will bring: Duties and Responsibilities: A. Teaching: Undergraduate and graduate instruction in counseling; develop and teach within undergraduate major in counseling; practicum supervision and participation in departmental clinic training activities; teach courses consistent with teaching expertise in relevant area. B. Research: Keep abreast of recent scholarly developments in areas of specialty and incorporate into teaching. Conduct and publish scholarly research. C. Service: Actively contribute to the intellectual and professional life of the Department, College of Health, Ball State University, and the surrounding community through general service. Participate in local and national professional service activities. Minimum Qualifications: Earned Doctorate in counseling psychology from APA accredited program by August 2026; ABD candidates will be considered only if all degree requirements will be completed by August 2026. The candidate must demonstrate professional competence in a specialty area within counseling psychology, and interest in teaching undergraduate courses and in teaching assessment. Preferred Qualifications: License-eligible as a Health Service Provider in Psychology. Highly qualified scholar with the ability to contribute to the department's scientist-professional training model, with demonstrated research, teaching and mentoring experiences and competencies, preferably at the undergraduate level. Special consideration will be given to candidates who can also contribute to one or more of the graduate programs in the department; with ability to mentor students, contribute, and facilitate immersive learning experiences.   How to apply: For inquiries regarding this vacancy, please contact: Dr. Nick Lee, at nicholas.lee@bsu.edu. Required documents: 1. Cover letter 2. Vitae (Do not use the Autofill resume feature) Optional documents: 1. Transcripts Consideration Date: to ensure full consideration, applications must be received by: November 29, 2025, at 12:01 A.M. (Applications will continue to be accepted after the full consideration date, until a sufficient applicant pool has been achieved or the position is filled. The closing date is subject to change without notice to applicants.) Employer will consider sponsorship. What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer 12 paid sick days and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Faculty and download our calculator spreadsheet."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Heat-Plant-Group-Leader_R-03244": {
      "title": "Heat Plant Group Leader",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-14\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Heat Plant Group Leader Compensation: $42.00 - $42.00 Department: Heat Plant Operations Start Date: 09/18/2026 About this opportunity: Ball State University Facilities Planning and Management has an opportunity to work on the beautiful campus. This opportunity comes with excellent pay and a great benefits package that includes medical and prescription plans, dental, flexible spending and health savings accounts, paid time off, holiday pay, university-funded retirement, tuition discounts, and more. The ideal candidate will be flexible, and will possess great service skills with a willingness to learn. This is a full-time, on campus opportunity. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. 3rd Shift 11:00 p.m. to 7:00 a.m. Sunday through Thursday What you'll do and what you'll bring: Position Function: Under general supervision, direct, lead, assign and perform duties related to inspection, maintenance, repair, replacement, and operation of all heat plant equipment, insuring compliance with EPA, OSHA, and all appropriate operating regulations and codes. Duties & Responsibilities: 1. Test water samples with chemicals and equipment; adjust chemical supplies in water depending on results of test. Requires the physical ability to stand, stoop, crouch, kneel, grasp, finger, lift, reach, climb, and exert in excess of 100 pounds of force occasionally, 50 pounds of force frequently, and 20 pounds of force constantly. Task requires the visual ability to read and interpret related Heating Plant instrumentation, perceive depth, and distinguish color. Task requires the ability to operate hand and power tools, ladders, scaffolds, related testing equipment, barrel truck, hand truck, etc. Employee is exposed to inside and outside environmental conditions, noise, dust, heights, confined spaces, and may be required to wear filter mask, respirator, and various protective clothing and/or equipment. Task requires the mental ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information, and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information. 2. Record tests and treatment data. Requires the physical ability to climb, balance, stoop, kneel, crouch, crawl, reach, finger, grasp, stand and/or walk for extended periods of time, and exert up to 10 pounds of force occasionally. Task requires the visual ability to perceive depth and distinguish color. Task requires the ability to operate related testing equipment. Employee is exposed to inside and outside environmental conditions, heights, and confined spaces. Task requires the mental ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information. 3. Assign and perform work related to maintenance, repair, and cleaning of the Heat Plant equipment. Requires the physical ability to climb, balance, stoop, kneel, crouch, crawl, reach, push, pull, lift, finger, grasp, talk, hear, stand and/or walk for extended periods of time, and exert in excess of 100 pounds of force occasionally, 50 pounds of force frequently, and 20 pounds of force constantly. Task requires the visual ability to perceive depth, read and interpret diagrams, schematics, and related Heating Plant instrumentation, and distinguish color. Task requires the ability to operate hand and power tools, ladders, scaffolds, welding machines, cutting torches, etc. Employee is exposed to inside and outside environmental conditions, extreme heat and cold, noise, dust, heights, confined spaces, and may be required to wear filter mask, respirator, and various protective clothing and/or equipment. Task requires the mental ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information. 4. Train Heat Plant staff in procedures for operation, maintenance, and repair of equipment. Requires the physical ability to climb, balance, stoop, kneel, crouch, crawl, reach, push, pull, lift, finger, grasp, talk, hear, stand and/or walk for extended periods of time, and exert in excess of 100 pounds of force occasionally, 50 pounds of force frequently, and 20 pounds of force constantly. Task requires the visual ability to perceive depth and read and interpret related Heating Plant instrumentation. Task requires the ability to operate hand and power tools, ladders, scaffolds, welding machines, cutting torches, related testing equipment, etc. Employee is exposed to inside and outside environmental conditions, extreme heat and cold, noise, dust, heights, confined spaces, and may be required to wear filter mask, respirator, and various protective clothing and/or equipment. Task requires the mental ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions, training reports, and information. 5. Inspect tunnels and equipment for condition and recommend maintenance projects Requires the physical ability to climb, balance, stoop, kneel, crouch, crawl, reach, push, pull, lift, finger, grasp, talk, hear, stand and/or walk for extended periods of time, and exert in excess of 100 pounds of force occasionally, 50 pounds of force frequently, and 20 pounds of force constantly. Task requires the visual ability to perceive depth and read and interpret related Heating Plant instrumentation. Task requires the ability to operate hand tools, ladders, and scaffolds. Employee is exposed to inside and outside environmental conditions, extreme heat and cold, noise, dust, heights, confined spaces, and may be required to wear filter mask, respirator, and various protective clothing and/or equipment. Task requires the mental ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information. 6. Acts for supervisor when assigned. Requires the physical ability to climb, balance, stoop, kneel, crouch, crawl, reach, push, pull, lift, finger, grasp, talk, hear, stand and/or walk for extended periods of time, and exert up to 100 pounds of force occasionally, up to 50 pounds of force frequently, and up to 20 pounds of force constantly. Task requires the visual ability to perceive depth, distinguish colors, and read and interpret related Heating Plant instrumentation. Task requires the ability to operate hand and power tools, ladders, scaffolds, office equipment, and computer keyboard. Employee is exposed to inside and outside environmental conditions, extreme heat and cold, noise, dust, heights, confined spaces, and may be required to wear filter mask, respirator, and various protective clothing and/or equipment. Task requires the mental ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information. 7. Evaluate and provide feedback on work performance of assigned employees. Requires the physical ability to walk, stand, talk, hear, grasp, finger, lift, and exert up to 10 pounds of force occasionally. Task requires the visual ability to perceive depth and distinguish color. Employee is exposed to inside environmental conditions. Task requires the mental ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information. 8. Acquire and maintain knowledge of various job related chemicals, environmental concerns, and current technological improvements/advancements. Requires the physical ability to walk, stand, talk, hear, grasp, finger, lift, and exert up to 10 pounds of force occasionally. Task requires the visual ability to read small print, perceive depth, and distinguish color. Employee is exposed to inside and outside environmental conditions. Task requires the mental ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information. 9. Read and comprehend blueprints, drawings, diagrams, and sketches to insure proper specifications are followed. Requires the physical ability to stand, talk, hear, and exert up to 10 pounds of force occasionally. Task requires the visual ability to distinguish color, read small print, and perceive depth. Employee is exposed to inside environmental conditions. Task requires the mental ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information. 10. Perform other duties as assigned. May require any or all of the above mentioned abilities. Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent (GED ). 1.Successful completion of an apprenticeship program as Stationary Engineer as approved by the Bureau of Apprenticeship and Training, or at least six (6) years of experience in operation and maintenance of a coal, gas, and oil fired boiler plant or related equipment, or equivalent combination of education and experience from which comparable job knowledge can be acquired as determined by Ball State University. 2.Must be able to read and comprehend all specified policies and procedures for safety, hazardous materials information, University policies, procedures, and communications, and perform mathematical calculations. 3.Must possess and maintain a valid Driver’s License and be insurable under the university’s auto fleet policy. . 4. Must be able to perform all mental and physical requirements as outlined in each job duty. 5.You must be 18 years or older. Preferred Qualifications: Vocational school training 1.Supervisory experience. 2. Over six (6) year’s experience. How to apply: For inquiries, please contact: Devon Johnson, Assistant Manager of Plant Operations at 765-285-6176 or devon.johnson@bsu.edu . Important:  Do not use the Autofill feature when uploading your resume. Optional documents (Recommended for best consideration). Resume Cover Letter detailing your qualifications for the position. What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer a generous paid time off program and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust short-term disability, long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. We do the same for you.  In fact, we'll cover 100 percent of the tuition costs for you to earn your undergraduate degree and 80 percent of your graduate tuition. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow.   Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Service and download our calculator spreadsheet."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Assistant-Teaching-Professor_R-03166-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Teaching Professor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-09\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Teaching Professor Compensation: $60,000-$65,000 Department: Physics & Astronomy Start Date: 08/16/2027 About this opportunity: An Assistant Teaching Professor of Physics faculty position is available starting August 2027. The successful application will be teaching primarily introductory courses for non-majors, though other courses may be needed as determined by the department chair and will participate in departmental service-related activities. Position eligible for yearly renewal with satisfactory progress. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you will bring: Duties and Responsibilities: The successful applicant will be expected to teach full-time (12 credit hours) lecture and laboratory courses primarily in the areas of introductory physics and astronomy. The successful applicant will contribute intellectual and professional service to the department at a level associated with contract-faculty-positions. Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. in physics, astronomy, physics education, or related discipline from an accredited institution by date of appointment. Teaching experience at the college level, which may include typical graduate assistantship assignments. Preferred Qualifications: Experience teaching introductory physics and/or astronomy courses for majors, non-majors, and/or pre-service elementary education majors. Effective communication skills in classroom and laboratory settings. How to apply: Search Committee Chair, Dr. John Millis, jpmillis@bsu.edu Please follow upload instructions to attach all of the required supporting documents listed below: NOTE: Do not use the Autofill feature for resume: Required Documents: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy and Interest Consideration Date: to ensure full consideration, applications must be received by November 19th, 2026. (Applications will continue to be accepted after the full consideration date, until a sufficient applicant pool has been achieved or the position is filled. The closing date is subject to change without notice to applicants.) What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer 12 paid sick days and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Faculty and download our calculator spreadsheet."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Assistant---Associate---Professor-of-Elementary-Education_R-03155": {
      "title": "Assistant / Associate / Professor of Elementary Education",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-15\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant / Associate / Professor of Elementary Education Compensation: $70,000 - $95,000 Department: Elementary Education Start Date: 08/02/2027 About this opportunity: Ball State University’s Department of Elementary Education invites applications for a full-time, tenure-line faculty position at the Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor rank beginning August 2027. While candidates at all ranks will be considered, we are particularly interested in applicants whose experiences and accomplishments support appointment at the Associate or Full Professor level. Salary range for Assistant Professor: $70,000 - $75,000 Salary range for Associate Professor or Professor: $75,000 - $95,000 We seek a collaborative teacher-scholar committed to preparing highly effective elementary educators and advancing knowledge in teaching and learning. The successful candidate will contribute to undergraduate and graduate programs in elementary education, with particular emphasis on literacy, inclusive teaching practices, and curriculum and instruction. We are especially interested in candidates whose teaching, scholarship, and professional engagement reflect current research and evidence-based practices in elementary education and who can contribute leadership to the department’s teaching, research, partnerships, and program development. This position offers opportunities to teach and mentor undergraduate and graduate students, supervise candidates in field-based settings, maintain a productive program of research and scholarship, collaborate with faculty and school/community partners, and contribute to the ongoing development of innovative educator preparation programs. Candidates at the Associate or Full Professor level should demonstrate a sustained record of scholarly productivity and professional contributions appropriate to rank. Employer will consider sponsorship. What you'll do and what you will bring: Duties and responsibilities :   Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in elementary education, with particular emphasis on literacy, inclusive teaching practices, and curriculum and instruction; supervise practicum and other field-based experiences; establish and maintain an active program of research and scholarly publication; pursue opportunities for external funding as appropriate; engage in partnerships with schools, families, communities, and other educational organizations; advise and mentor graduate students, including doctoral students; collaborate with faculty on program development and improvement; provide leadership appropriate to experience and rank; and provide professional university, college, and departmental service. Salary range for Assistant Professor: $70,000 - $75,000 Salary range for Associate Professor or Professor: $75,000 - $95,000      Minimum Qualifications:    Earned doctorate in Elementary Education, Literacy, Curriculum and Instruction, or closely related field from an accredited institution by the date of appointment.  At least three years (6 academic semesters/24 months) of teaching experience in an elementary (K-6) setting  Demonstrated record of scholarly productivity, as evidenced by refereed presentations at regional, national, or international conferences and/or scholarly publications such as refereed journal articles, book chapters, or books.  For appointment at the Associate or Full Professor level, a record of teaching, scholarship, and service commensurate with expectations for the respective rank.  Preferred Qualifications:    University-level teaching experience (at least one academic semester/3 months).  Expertise literacy instruction and knowledge of current research and evidence-based approaches to literacy teaching, including developments associated with the Science of Reading.   Knowledge of, and experience with, using current approaches to inclusive teaching, culturally responsive and sustaining pedagogies, and/or equitable educational practice while teaching learners with a wide range of strengths, needs, experiences, and backgrounds  Experience supervising preservice teachers or other educator candidates in field-based settings.  Demonstrated commitment to and experience with partnerships involving schools, families, communities, and/or community agencies.  Record of seeking and/or obtaining external grant funding.  Experience effectively integrating educational technologies into teaching, including online or technology-enhanced instruction.  Evidence of effective collaboration with colleagues and other educational partners.  For candidates at the Associate or Full Professor level, evidence of leadership in one or more areas such as program development, curriculum innovation, graduate education, research initiatives, externally funded projects, professional organizations, or school and community partnerships.  Experience mentoring graduate students, doctoral students, and/or early-career faculty  A sustained record of scholarly productivity and professional engagement appropriate to rank.   Required License/Certifications: How to apply: For inquiries about this opportunity, please contact: ELED Department Chairperson, Jackie Sydnor jtsydnor@bsu.edu   Important: Please follow upload instructions for attaching all required documents listed below. Only complete applications will be considered. REQUIRED APPLICATION DOCUMENTS: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Within the application, you will be asked to provide names and contact information for three (3) professional references. This position will remain open until filled with a consideration date of October 19, 2026, 12:01 a.m. Candidates submitting application materials on or before this date will receive full consideration. Review of applications will continue until the position is filled. What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer 12 paid sick days and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Faculty and download our calculator spreadsheet."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Assistant-Professor-of-Elementary-Education_R-03168-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Elementary Education",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-15\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Professor of Elementary Education Compensation: $70,000 - $75,000 Department: Elementary Education Start Date: 08/02/2027 About this opportunity: Ball State University’s Department of Elementary Education welcomes applications for a full-time tenure-track Assistant Professor available August 2027. We seek a collaborative teacher-scholar committed to preparing highly effective elementary educators and advancing knowledge in teaching and learning. The successful candidate will contribute to undergraduate and graduate programs in elementary education, with particular emphasis on literacy, inclusive teaching practices, and curriculum and instruction. We are especially interested in candidates whose teaching, scholarship, and professional engagement reflect current research and evidence-based practices in elementary education and who are committed to meaningful partnerships with schools and communities. This position offers opportunities to teach and mentor undergraduate and graduate students, supervise candidates in field-based settings, develop a productive program of research and scholarship, collaborate with faculty and school/community partners, and contribute to the ongoing development of innovative educator preparation programs. Employer will consider sponsorship. What you'll do and what you will bring: Duties and responsibilities :  Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in elementary education, with particular emphasis on literacy, inclusive teaching practices, and curriculum and instruction; supervise practicum and other field-based experiences; establish and maintain an active program of research and scholarly publication; pursue opportunities for external funding as appropriate; engage partnerships with schools, families, communities, and other educational organizations; advise and mentor graduate students, including doctoral students; collaborate with faculty on program development and improvement; and provide professional university, college, and departmental service.  Minimum Qualifications: Earned doctorate in Elementary Education, Literacy, Curriculum and Instruction, or closely related field from an accredited institution by the date of appointment.  At least three years (6 academic semesters/24 months) of teaching experience in an elementary (K-6) setting.  Demonstrated potential for or record of scholarly productivity, as evidenced by refereed presentations at regional, national, or international conferences and/or scholarly publications such as refereed journal articles, book chapters, or books.  Preferred Qualifications: University-level teaching experience (at least one academic semester/3 months).  Expertise in literacy instruction and knowledge of current research and evidence-based approaches to literacy teaching, including developments associated with the Science of Reading.   Knowledge of, and experience with, using current approaches to inclusive teaching, culturally responsive and sustaining pedagogies, and/or equitable educational practice while teaching learners with a wide range of strengths, needs, experiences, and backgrounds  Experience supervising pre-service teachers or other educator candidates in field-based settings.  Demonstrated commitment to and experience with partnerships involving schools, families, communities, and/or community agencies.  Record of seeking and/or obtaining external grant funding.  Experience effectively integrating educational technologies into teaching, including online or technology-enhanced instruction.  Evidence of effective collaboration with colleagues and other educational partners.  Required Certifications: How to apply: For inquiries about this opportunity, please contact: Elementary Education Department Chairperson, Jackie Sydnor jtsydnor@bsu.edu   Important: Please follow upload instructions for attaching all required documents listed below. Only complete applications will be considered. REQUIRED APPLICATION DOCUMENTS Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy References: Within the application, you will be prompted to provide the names and contact information for three (3) professional references. This position will remain open until filled with a consideration date of October 19, 2026, 12:01 a.m. Candidates submitting application materials on or before this date will receive full consideration. Review of applications will continue until the position is filled. What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer 12 paid sick days and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Faculty and download our calculator spreadsheet."
