    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Instructors-of-Journalism-and-Strategic-Communication_R-03338": {
      "title": "Instructors of Journalism and Strategic Communication",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-23\nPart time\n\nPosition Title:   Instructors of Journalism and Strategic Communication Compensation: $3,000 per three-credit hour class Department: School of Journalism & Stratgc Comm - Temp Start Date: 01/11/2027 About this opportunity:   The School of Journalism and Strategic Communication is a supportive community of faculty, staff, and students driven to pursue knowledge and share truth that spurs progress and adds value to our world. Our faculty are expert researchers and practitioners in journalism and strategic communication dedicated to outfitting students with the expertise, confidence, and connections to lead our fields. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring:   Position Function: The School of Journalism and Strategic Communication invites applications for part-time instructors to teach online and/or on-campus, undergraduate and/or graduate courses beginning in January 2027 in advertising, journalism, media analytics, AI, public relations, sports public relations, design and/or photo journalism.     Duties and Responsibilities: Teach online and/or on-campus, undergraduate and/or graduate courses beginning in Spring 2027 in advertising, journalism, media analytics, AI, public relations, sports public relations, design and/or photojournalism.  Minimum Qualifications: Master’s degree from an accredited college or university in advertising, journalism, public relations, sports administration, mass communications, or field related to the classes taught by the date of appointment. OR A Bachelor’s Degree and evidence demonstrating a high level of professional proficiency and expertise in advertising, journalism, public relations, sports public relations, mass communications, or field related to the classes taught by the date of appointment. Evidence may include: (1) high-quality portfolio and/or résumé including 5+ years of experience in relation to courses to be taught;(2) evidence of leadership/management experience and/or evidence of professional experience in highly competitive professional media environments;(3) nationally recognized license or certification;(4) significant professional awards; OR(5) high-quality peer-reviewed scholarly and/or juried creative activities.         Preferred Qualifications:           Terminal degree from an accredited college or university in advertising, journalism, public relations, mass communications, or related field relevant to the classes taught; five years teaching experience; and five years professional media experience. How to apply:   Dr. Johnny Sparks, Director and Professor-Committee Chair; jvsparks@bsu.edu Please follow upload instructions to attach all of the required supporting documents listed below: IMPORTANT: To ensure accurate processing of your application, do not rely on a resume upload to populate the job experience section. All work history must be entered directly into the application fields. Three references will need to be provided. Required Documents: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae (CV)"
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Assistant-Professor-of-Information-Systems-and-Operations-Management_R-03186": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Information Systems and Operations Management",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-23\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Professor of Information Systems and Operations Management Compensation: $130,000-$135,000 Department: Info Systems & Operations Mgt (Qiannong Start Date: 08/02/2027 About this opportunity: The Department of Information Systems and Operations Management in the Miller College of Business at Ball State University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position beginning August 2027. Candidates with an interest and ability to teach undergraduate and/or graduate business analytics and information systems courses and conduct quality research in the same fields are encouraged to apply. Employer will consider sponsorship. What you'll do and what you will bring: Duties and Responsibilities: Responsibilities: teaching nine semester hours each fall and spring semester in subjects such as but not limited to: business analytics, Information Systems, Networking, Database, cyber security, AI in business; assignment may include undergraduate and graduate courses, which may be delivered on-line, synchronously or asynchronously. Additional activities will include scholarly activity and service. ​ Minimum Qualifications: Earned doctorate in Business Analytics and Information Systems or closely related fields from an accredited institution. Candidates with ABD will be considered and must demonstrate satisfactory progress toward completion of the doctoral degree consistent with university policy. Evidence of, or demonstrated potential for high-quality scholarly research and effective university-level teaching. Preferred Qualifications: Record of scholarly publications in peer-reviewed quality journals; experience in creative teaching methods such as experiential-learning, service-learning, immersive-learning, or other instructional innovations; and on-line teaching; evidence of active involvement in external grant writing; business experience in the field of Information Systems or related areas; ability to teach and conduct research in Business Analytics and Information Systems. How to apply: For inquiries about this opportunity, please contact: Department Chair, Dr. Qiannong Gu, qgu@bsu.edu Important: Please follow upload instructions for attaching all required documents listed below. Only complete applications will be considered. REQUIRED APPLICATION DOCUMENTS Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae (Do not use the Autofill resume feature.) References: Within the application, you will be prompted to provide the names and contact information for three (3) professional references. Optional Documents: Teaching Evaluations Teaching Philosophy Applications must be received before 12:01 AM on October 28, 2026. What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer 12 paid sick days and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Faculty and download our calculator spreadsheet."
