    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Assistant-Director-of-Student-Success_R-02450": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Student Success",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-28\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Director of Student Success Compensation: $50,000-55,000 Department: CSH Deans Office_F About this opportunity: Reporting to the Assistant Dean and Director of Student Success, the Assistant Director of Student Success is responsible for developing and implementing programs, partnerships, and resources to support students’ academic success and career readiness for our nearly 70 distinct majors in the College of Sciences and Humanities (CSH) with the goal of increasing student retention and success for our more than nearly 4,000 undergraduate majors. The Assistant Director is responsible for the daily operations of the growing CSH Success Hub that sees more than 3,000 student visits each semester. What you'll do and what you'll bring: Primary Responsibilities Interacts with and supports students at programs and events and through individual scheduled and drop-in sessions to discuss areas of concern. Assists in the planning and execution of targeted, innovative and evidence-based programs and services for students aimed at improving student success and retention with emphasis on academic support and career readiness. Supports the Assistant Dean to coordinate recruitment and orientation activities including prospective undergraduate student visits, admissions events such as Cardinal Preview Days, CSH Preview Day, Admitted Student Day, and orientation programs. Assists with the college’s Welcome Week activities with our academic departments in collaboration with the Associate Dean and Assistant Dean. Works with campus partners and stakeholders for cross-departmental student success initiatives, providing information, securing space reservations, scheduling planning meetings, and providing necessary documentation and reports. Partners with the Assistant Dean and CSH Dean’s Communications Team to develop annual CSH Success Hub marketing plan, promotional materials, and publications, and maintains update-to-date content on the CSH Success Hub website. Manages, and creates content for, the CSH Success Hub’s social media and Canvas Community platforms. Utilizes BSU technology platforms to document student support, track attendance at CSH Success Hub events/programs, conduct student outreach, respond to Navigate alerts, and analyze trends. Recruits, supervises, and evaluates the activities and performance of CSH Success Hub graduate assistant and undergraduate employees including onboarding, training, assigning and reviewing work in collaboration with the Assistant Dean. Facilitates the assessment and evaluation of CSH’s student retention and success initiatives. Assists with the preparation of post-program/event reports and the CSH Success Hub Year-in-Review report. Represents the college on select university committees as needed. Supports the mission, values, and goals of Ball State University and the College of Sciences and Humanities. Other duties as requested by the Assistant Dean. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in psychology, education, sociology, or related field by date of hire. At least 3 years of experience working in education, nonprofit, or related field. Experience planning small and large-scale events for a diverse population of stakeholders, such as students, faculty, families, alumni, and/or donors. Display independent, professional judgment and organizational skills to plan, prioritize, and manage a diverse workload with sensitivity and confidentiality while maintaining accuracy with the many details. Ability to gather, analyze, and interpret data as well as creatively solve problems. Ability to work independently as well as collaboratively within a team and assume responsibility for problem-solving. Strong communication, administrative, and presentation skills. Resounding commitment to excellence and genuine care for student success. Proficiency in Microsoft Office, Word, Excel, PowerPoint, and other common software packages. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree in a related field with at least 4 years of related work experience in higher education or related field. Knowledge of and experience with student success, admissions, advising, and/or student developmental theory. Supervisory experience in higher education, especially in student-facing roles. How to apply: For inquiries, please contact: College of Sciences and Humanities Dean's office at 765-285-1042. Please follow upload instructions to attach all of the required supporting documents listed below: NOTE: Do not use the Autofill feature for resume: Cover letter Resume Applications must be received by October 12th, 2026, at 12:01 AM.  What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer paid 24 vacation days, 12 sick days and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. We do the same for you.  In fact, we'll cover 100 percent of the tuition costs for you to earn your undergraduate degree and 80 percent of your graduate tuition.  This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Professional and download the spreadsheet. If you are applying for a 10-month position or one with Burris or Indiana Academy, please select the corresponding calculator."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Travel-Specialist_R-03303": {
      "title": "Travel Specialist",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-28\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Travel Specialist Compensation: $16.50 - 17.84 Department: Accounts Payable_A (Samantha Rowe Start Date: 10/26/2026 About this opportunity: Join our Accounts Payable – Travel team in a dynamic role that combines customer service, financial review, technology, policy administration, and problem-solving. As a Travel Specialist, you’ll serve as a key resource for University employees, helping travelers and departments navigate the University’s travel processes from pre-approval and booking through reimbursement and reconciliation. In this role, you’ll review and approve travel pre-approvals, expense reports, cash advances, and travel bookings while ensuring expenses comply with University policies. You’ll assist with airfare, hotel, conference registrations, and other travel arrangements; audit travel purchasing card activity; and follow up on outstanding cash advances. You’ll also help travelers resolve complex or time-sensitive situations when plans change or issues arise. Technology and communication are a big part of this position. You’ll work in multiple travel and financial systems, troubleshoot software and booking issues, monitor the Travel email account, collaborate with departments and travel vendors, and help test system updates and improvements. You’ll also have opportunities to contribute to Travel Policy reviews, develop training materials, and communicate important travel updates to the campus community. We’re looking for someone who is detail-oriented, organized, comfortable making decisions, and committed to providing excellent customer service—even when situations are time-sensitive or complex. If you enjoy solving problems, working with technology, interpreting policies, and helping people navigate processes, this is an opportunity to build your expertise in University travel while making an impact across campus. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the United States without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring: Position Function: Serve as a resource to the university on all travel questions and issues; administer and enforce university travel regulations and policies; approve or deny all pre-approvals and expense reports; resolve travel issues and technical issues; respond to high-pressure and time-sensitive situations; approve or deny all travel bookings through the university’s travel software. Audit travel cards monthly. Duties & Responsibilities: 1. Serve as a resource for all university travel; communicate with travelers, departments, travel agencies, and other outside entities through various mediums; resolve complex travel issues while complying with university travel policies. 2. Review all travel bookings through the university’s dedicated travel booking tool for compliance, accuracy, and price thresholds; approve bookings in a timely manner to ensure best rate and reservations; update booking software with user information; grant and track access to university travel card(s) for select bookings, and make other updates as needed. 3. Review pre-approvals and cash advance requests submitted for accuracy and to ensure travel-related expenditures are in compliance with travel policies; approve/deny/return for correction and discuss with supervisor as needed. 4. Pay conference registrations, airfare, hotel, etc., using the travel purchasing card. Book various forms of travel in situations where departmental purchasing cards cannot be used for conference registrations or situations where the university’s dedicated booking tool cannot be used and ensure all bookings comply with university travel policies. 5. Review/audit expense reports and cash advance reconciliations submitted for accuracy and to ensure travel-related expenditures are in compliance with travel policies; review all details and resolve discrepancies and complex issues; verify mileage and calculate per diems; approve/deny/return for correction and discuss with supervisor as needed. 6. Perform the following duties pertaining to cash advances: retrieve report of weekly outstanding cash advances; send weekly emails to travelers with overdue cash advances and follow up until advance has cleared. 7. Coordinate review of the University Travel Policy quarterly by both Travel Specialists and update as needed. Assist in the creation of training materials/videos related to travel. Communicate any changes to the University Travel Policy to the campus community. 8. Maintain travel email account; respond to questions and provide guidance for all travel-related questions. 9. Assist with troubleshooting and resolving travel software issues, including communicating with software vendors, departments, and external customers. Participate in software testing as needed. Review daily feeds/reports and resolve issues as needed for travel systems. 10. Review and approve/deny travel access requests and update appropriate access in various university travel systems. 11. Complete monthly audits of departmental credit cards for assigned cards and all travel card usage; verify all receipts are received in a timely fashion; audit receipts to determine appropriate university expenditures; communicate with cardholders/proxies as required. 12. Perform other related duties as assigned. 13. Maintain regular and predictable attendance. Minimum Qualifications: Associate’s degree or equivalent in accounting or other business-related field. Over three through five years of accounting, accounts payable, auditing, or other detailed administrative experience. Excellent Microsoft Office and organization skills. Preferred Qualifications: Over three years of accounting experience. Experience processing travel reimbursements/payments. How to apply: Questions regarding this position may be directed to: Samantha Rowe Director of Accounts Payable srowe@bsu.edu Please apply via the online Ball State University job portal . Please list three professional references within the online application. Supporting Documents Upload Instructions: Important:  Do  not  use the Autofill feature when uploading your resume. Please follow the upload instructions to attach the required supporting document listed below. Required Document: Resume Optional Document: Cover Letter What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer paid 10 to 24 vacation days, 12 sick days, and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. We do the same for you.  In fact, we'll cover 100 percent of the tuition costs for you to earn your undergraduate degree and 80 percent of your graduate tuition.  This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that show you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Staff (Exempt) and download our calculator spreadsheet."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Instructor-of-Urban-Planning_R-03347": {
      "title": "Instructor of Urban Planning",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-28\nPart time\n\nPosition Title:   Instructor of Urban Planning Compensation: $1,500 - $9,000 Department: Urban Planning - Temp Start Date: 01/03/2027 About this opportunity:   The Department of Urban Planning seeks part-time professionals to teach several urban planning courses during spring semester. This is not a full-time position. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring:   Position Description: These part-time adjunct instructors will teach either one course to undergraduate and graduate students in the Department of Urban Planning or teach or co-teach a studio class. Duties and responsibilities will include providing timely feedback and midterm grades to students. Minimum Qualifications: The candidate must hold a a master's degree in urban planning or a closely aligned field or a bachelor's degree with at least four years' experience working in the planning field. Two part-time positions require some experience with studio classes, whether as a student or a faculty member. Preferred Qualifications: Preferably a PhD or a master's with experience working as a professional planner. How to apply:   For inquiries, please contact: jhwest@bsu.edu Please follow upload instructions to attach all of the required supporting documents listed below: NOTE: Do not use the Autofill feature for resume. Required Documents: 1. Curriculum Vitae 2. Contact information for 3 references Optional: 1. Cover Letter Please bundle your documents into one document to ensure that you can include all required items."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Instructor-of-Music--Commercial-Voice-_R-03342-1": {
      "title": "Instructor of Music (Commercial Voice)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-28\nPart time\n\nPosition Title:   Instructor of Music (Commercial Voice) Compensation: $500 - $9,000 Department: School of Music - Temp Start Date: 01/10/2027 About this opportunity:   Ball State School of Music is seeking to hire one adjunct instructor to teach applied contemporary/commercial voice lessons in the Spring 2027 semester. Candidates must be have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring:   Job Description: Ball State is seeking to hire one adjunct instructor to teach applied contemporary/commercial voice lessons in the Spring 2027 semester. Lessons are held on campus, and individual times are scheduled between the instructor and each student in accordance with the student's class schedule and the instructor's availability.  Qualifications: Experience teaching/coaching and performing a variety of contemporary/commercial musical styles (R&B, soul, jazz, gospel, country/folk, pop, rock, etc.), including the use of a microphone for amplification. How to apply:   Required Documents: 1. Cover Letter 2. Curriculum Vitae (Do Not use the \"Autofill\" resume feature) Optional Documents: 1. Master's Transcripts 2. Doctorate Transcripts Interested instructors may contact Professor Justin DeLong, Assistant Teaching Professor of Commercial Voice and Musical Theatre, at justin.delong@bsu.edu for information about the position. Review of applications will start: 11/1/2026"
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Assistant-Professor-of-Studio-Art--Printmaking-_R-03273": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Studio Art (Printmaking)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-29\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Professor of Studio Art (Printmaking) Compensation: $56,000 - $62,000 Department: School of Art Start Date: 08/15/2027 About this opportunity: The School of Art at Ball State University welcomes applications for a full-time, tenure-line Assistant Professor of Studio Art with a specialty in printmaking. The ideal candidate will be a creative teacher, thoughtful mentor, and collaborative colleague who will foster interdisciplinary collaboration across the School of Art's many studio areas. The School of Art has over forty full-time faculty and staff and offers state-of-the-art facilities serving approximately 700 undergraduate majors. Programs at the BA, BS, and BFA levels include art education, art history, graphic design, graphic design studies, animation production, illustration, game art/design, visual effects, and a studio art program that includes drawing, painting, printmaking, ceramics, glass, metals + jewelry, sculpture, photography, and video and new media. School of Art students enjoy world-class facilities, with over 73,000 square feet of classroom, gallery, and studio space in the Art and Journalism Building, Applied Technology Building, and the Marilyn K. Glick Center for Glass. Students and faculty work closely with David Owsley Museum of Art on campus, among the finest university art collections in the nation. Ball State University is accredited by the National Association for Schools of Art and Design.   Teaching responsibilities are on campus, in Muncie, Indiana.   This position is open until filled with a priority consideration date of November 10, 2026. Candidates submitting application materials on or before this date will receive full consideration.  Employer will consider sponsorship. What you'll do and what you will bring: Description:    Tenure-line faculty in the School of Art teach undergraduate courses at all levels, from first-year Foundations through senior projects. They also pursue creative and scholarly research in their field by exhibiting, publishing, and presenting their work professionally. All faculty participate in service at the School, College, and University level and are committed to student success and curricular innovation.       Duties and Responsibilities:    -Courses are generally scheduled on campus, with occasional courses scheduled online, either synchronously or asynchronously.    -Instructional load will include all levels of course work in classes such as:     ADS 101 2D Foundations   AFA 231 Printmaking: Introduction   AFA 341 Printmaking: Intaglio   AFA 351 Printmaking: Lithography   AFA 361 Printmaking: Relief   AFA 371 Printmaking: Serigraphy   AFA 381 Bookmaking   AFA 298 Special Topics in Studio Art   AFA 398 Advanced Studio Art    AFA 498 Seminar in Fine Arts    ART 437 Professional Practices for Studio Artists    AFA 490 Studio Senior Project    -Other teaching duties based on programmatic need and the expertise of the faculty hired individual may be assigned.   -Additional responsibilities include course development and maintaining studios and equipment in collaboration with other faculty and staff   -Tenure-line faculty are responsible for producing scholarship/creative work commensurate with the requirements for tenure.   -Contribute to and participate in the life and development of the School of Art, the College of Fine Arts, and the University by serving on committees and being active in their discipline’s community.   Minimum Qualifications:    Master of Fine Arts (MFA) degree in art, design, or related field from an accredited institution by date of appointment.    Ability to develop curriculum and facilities for printmaking.   One semester of teaching experience at the college level, gained concurrently or at any time.       Preferred Qualifications:    Evidence of professional engagement through exhibitions, publications, residencies, grants, commissions, collaborations, curatorial projects, and/or community-based projects.   Ability to teach in a secondary studio area including but not limited to drawing, painting, photography, video and new media, sculpture, ceramics, metals + jewelry, or glass.   Ability to contribute to a forward-looking and interdisciplinary studio art program.   One year of teaching experience at the college level, gained concurrently or at any time.   How to apply: How to apply :   For inquiries regarding this opportunity, please contact:   Lara Kuykendall, Director,  lkuykendall@bsu.edu        Please follow upload instructions to attach one PDF of all of the required supporting documents listed below. NOTE: Do not use the Autofill feature for resume.  Cover Letter   Curriculum Vitae   Sample syllabi for two college-level art courses  Portfolio of 10 to 20 examples of applicant’s creative work (with links to time-based work if applicable). If document size exceeds 10 MB, a link to portfolio may be provided.   Portfolio of 10 to 20 examples of student projects (with links to time-based work if applicable). If document size exceeds 10 MB, a link to portfolio may be provided.    Contact information (including email addresses) for three professional references   The position will remain open until filled with a priority consideration date of November 10, 2026. Candidates submitting application materials on or before this date will receive full consideration.    What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer 12 paid sick days and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Faculty and download our calculator spreadsheet."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Foundation-Fund-Accountant_R-03383": {
      "title": "Foundation Fund Accountant",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-02\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Foundation Fund Accountant Compensation: $50,000 - $55,000 Department: BSU Foundation_G About this opportunity: Join Our Team: Foundation Fund Accountant Are you ready to be part of an energetic and unified team dedicated to transforming higher education? Our foundation is breaking down barriers between advancement, alumni relations, and stewardship to create a cohesive environment where philanthropy and innovative partnerships thrive. This is your chance to make a significant impact as we fulfill Our Call to Beneficence: The Campaign for Ball State University, aimed at elevating student support both financially and academically. Why Join Us? -Dynamic Team Environment: Collaborate with passionate professionals who are committed to our mission. -Cutting-Edge Initiatives: Be at the forefront of redefining philanthropy in education. -Unified Structure: Work within a seamless organization with no barriers between key departments. -Supportive Culture: A high-achieving work environment that values camaraderie and collaboration. -Impactful Work: A mission that changes lives through education and philanthropy. We invite you to join our team and make a difference. Join us in our mission to support students in realizing their purpose, achieving their dreams, and leading meaningful lives. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring: Position Function: Provide accounting, fund administration, financial operations, and stewardship support to the Foundation Finance Team for the Ball State University Foundation and its related entities. This position is responsible for monitoring and administering Foundation funds, ensuring compliance with donor intent and fund agreements, and Foundation policies. Responsibilities include reviewing and processing fund disbursements, supporting financial reporting and audit activities, maintaining effective internal controls and assisting in the stewardship of Foundation assets. The successful candidate will apply accounting principles, analytical skills, sound judgement, and a strong service orientation to support the Foundation’s fiduciary responsibilities and financial operations. Duties and Responsibilities: Administer fund disbursement withdrawal requests and serve as a steward of Foundation funds. Review withdrawal and payment requests for accuracy, fund availability, compliance with donor intent, fund agreements, and Foundation policies. Analyze, reconcile, and validate charges to ensure appropriate allocation and accounting. Record transactions in the financial system, coordinate payment processing, monitor cash requirements, and communicate with vendors and internal stakeholders regarding disbursement-related matters for all entities. Provide supporting documentation to the Office of the University Controller on a monthly basis. Interpret, analyze, and monitor Foundation fund agreements and related documentation to ensure expenditures and financial activity adhere to donor intent, fund restrictions, and available balances. Provide guidance and information to Foundation staff, campus partners, and other stakeholders regarding Foundation related transactions and procedures. Prepare and maintain weekly and monthly cash flow projections related to fund disbursement and Foundation operating activities. Communicate regularly with the Foundation Controller regarding cash needs and funding requirements. Support administration of Foundation credit card program by reviewing expenditures for business purpose, policy compliance, proper documentation, and accurate accounting treatment. Research discrepancies, resolve issues, and communicate with cardholders as needed. Assist with the administration of the unclaimed property process for all entities, including monitoring outstanding items, processing voids and reissues, supporting state reporting requirements, and ensuring compliance with applicable laws and regulations. Support annual Form 1099 reporting for all entities by reviewing vendor activity, analyzing transactions, validating classifications, and maintaining compliance with federal reporting requirements. Support annual external audit and other compliance reviews by preparing documentation, responding to information requests, and maintaining audit-ready records in accordance with accounting standards and Foundation policies. Identify, recommend, develop, and implement process improvements that enhance operational efficiency, strengthen internal controls, improve reporting accuracy, and support effective fund administration. Maintain written procedures and documentation related to assigned responsibilities. Provide operational support to the Foundation Finance Team, including preparing correspondence, reports, and communications for internal and external partners. Perform other related accounting, financial, fund management and administrative duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in Finance, Business, or Accounting (or related) from an accredited institution, or equivalent combination of education and experience. Additional Preferred Qualifications: At least two years of experience in computer systems, accounting applications and related software, and databases Knowledge of/experience with not-for-profit organizations and fund accounting Excellent verbal and written communication skills; proficient with Microsoft Excel. How to apply: How to Apply:   For inquiries, please contact: Amy McClure at almcclure@bsu.edu   Please follow upload instructions to attach all of the required supporting documents listed below.    Supporting Documents Upload Instructions: Important: Do not use the Autofill feature when uploading your resume.   Required Document: Resume   Optional Document (Recommended for best consideration): Cover Letter detailing your qualifications for the position. What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer paid 24 vacation days, 12 sick days and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. We do the same for you.  In fact, we'll cover 100 percent of the tuition costs for you to earn your undergraduate degree and 80 percent of your graduate tuition.  This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Professional and download the spreadsheet. If you are applying for a 10-month position or one with Burris or Indiana Academy, please select the corresponding calculator."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Assistant-Professor-of-Architecture_R-03339": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Architecture",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-01\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Professor of Architecture Compensation: $70,000 - $75,000 Department: Architecture Start Date: 08/16/2027 About this opportunity: Ball State University’s Department of Architecture seeks faculty candidates for a tenure track position at the rank of Assistant Professor available starting in August 2027. Major responsibilities lie mainly within the area of design studio instruction at both the undergraduate and graduate levels as well as lecture/seminar courses in the candidate's areas of focus. Candidates should also be able to demonstrate a record of current and advanced design methods with the ability to teach—and speak to—contemporary design processes and effective visual communication and representation strategies. Our faculty are collegial, collaborative, innovative, inclusive, and adaptive, both within and beyond one’s home unit. These attributes include commitments to collaborative discourse, interdisciplinary inquiry, and enterprising learning practices. Our faculty are expected to be innovative, adaptive, engaging teachers across modalities; producers of impactful creative and/or scholarly work; leaders in meaningful service activities to multiple communities. We seek faculty members who are strategic thinkers, engaging our dynamic communities. We are committed to student and faculty success, impact, and access, within an environment that prioritizes inclusive excellence. We inspire each other to be critical thinkers and responsible citizens, so that we can pursue fulfilling careers and meaningful lives. Ball State University lives the values of Beneficence. We invite you to be part of our community. Ball State University is located in Muncie, Indiana, on an attractive campus 45 miles northeast of Indianapolis. Approximately 20,000 graduate and undergraduate students enroll in one of eight academic colleges that offer 270+ undergraduate and graduate programs. Many of our master’s, doctoral, certificate, and specialist degrees rank among the best in the nation. We engage students in educational, research, and creative endeavors that empower our graduates to have fulfilling careers and meaningful lives enriched by lifelong learning and service, while we enhance the economic, environmental, and social vitality of our community, our state, and our world. Employer will consider sponsorship. Position will remain open until filled. To ensure full consideration, applications must be received by January 1, 2027. (Applications will continue to be accepted after the full consideration date, until a sufficient applicant pool has been achieved or the position if filled. The closing date is subject to change without notice to applicants.) What you'll do and what you will bring: Position Function: Ball State University’s Department of Architecture seeks faculty candidates for a tenure track position at the rank of Assistant Professor available starting in August 2027. Major responsibilities lie mainly within the area of design studio instruction at both the undergraduate and graduate levels as well as lecture/seminar courses in the candidate's areas of focus. Candidates should also be able to demonstrate a record of current and advanced design methods with the ability to teach—and speak to—contemporary design processes and effective visual communication and representation strategies. The Estopinal College of Architecture and Planning (CAP) at Ball State University has a rich history in community engaged, professionally grounded, innovative, and impactful design education. The Department of Architecture offers undergraduate and graduate architecture programs that emphasize the education of architecture students through design studio, engagement with social and environmental issues, immersive and experiential learning, digital fluency and design computation, high performance building design, building systems and assemblies, historic preservation, digital fabrication, and critical practice in the pursuit of preparing the next generation of leaders in architecture. Duties & Responsibilities: This position carries a standard 12-credit academic workload per semester, structured as a 9-credit teaching load (typically one studio plus a 3-credit course) and a 3-credit research allocation dedicated to active scholarship and publication. Minimum Qualifications: 1. Master of Architecture degree by time of appointment OR; 2. Bachelor of Architecture degree with post-professional master’s degree in architecture or allied discipline from an accredited college or university by time of appointment. Preferred Qualifications: Professional licensure in architecture OR; a PhD in architecture. Evidence of excellence in teaching within an architectural curriculum; evidence of productive scholarship (research/creative work) with an active research, grant solicitation, and publication agenda; a track record of excellence in professional practice and service; design studio teaching; excellence and experience in teaching a primary AND secondary topical area. How to apply: For inquiries, please contact: Sarah Keogh - shkeogh@bsu.edu Please following upload instructions to attach all the required supporting documents listed below. Note: Do not use the Auto fill feature for resume: Cover Letter Resume/ Curriculum Vitae Portfolio License/Certification - Optional Position will remain open until filled. To ensure full consideration, applications must be received by January 1, 2027. (Applications will continue to be accepted after the full consideration date, until a sufficient applicant pool has been achieved or the position if filled. The closing date is subject to change without notice to applicants.) What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer 12 paid sick days and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Faculty and download our calculator spreadsheet."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Assistant-Lecturer-Assistant-Teaching-Professor_R-03234": {
      "title": "Assistant Lecturer/Assistant Teaching Professor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-05\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Lecturer/Assistant Teaching Professor Compensation: $45,000-$50,000 Department: Women's & Gender Studies (African American Studies) Start Date: 08/16/2027 About this opportunity: Ball State University welcomes applications for an Assistant Lecturer/Assistant Teaching Professor. This is a non-tenure-line, renewable position with a specialization in African American Studies and Women’s and Gender Studies. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you will bring: Duties and Responsibilities: This is a non-tenure-line, renewable position with a specialization in African American Studies and Women’s and Gender Studies. Responsibilities include teaching four sections per semester of courses, including but not limited to AFAM 100 (Introduction to African American Studies), AFAM 150 (Understanding Race, Antiracism and Intersectionality), WGS 210 (Introduction to Women’s and Gender Studies), and WGS 220 (International Women’s Issues), with the opportunity to teach upper-level courses in the African American Studies program and Women’s and Gender Studies program. Minimum Qualifications: Master’s Degree in African American Studies, Women’s and Gender Studies, or in a related field by date of appointment. Preferred Qualifications : ABD or Ph.D. in African American Studies, Women’s and Gender Studies, or in a related field with an active research agenda focusing on intersectionality and previous teaching (online and in person). How to apply: For inquiries, please contact: Dr. Sharon Jones ( Search Committee Chair) at sharon.jones@bsu.edu Please follow upload instructions to attach all of the required supporting documents listed below: NOTE: Do not use the Autofill feature for resume: Cover Letter CV Teaching Evaluations Teaching Philosophy Statement Consideration Date: to ensure full consideration, applications must be received by November 4th, 2026. (Applications will continue to be accepted after the full consideration date, until a sufficient applicant pool has been achieved or the position is filled. The closing date is subject to change without notice to applicants.) What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer 12 paid sick days and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Faculty and download our calculator spreadsheet."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Accounting-Specialist-for-Housing-and-Residence-Life_R-03422": {
      "title": "Accounting Specialist for Housing and Residence Life",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Accounting Specialist for Housing and Residence Life Salary Grade: Staff 10 Compensation: $16.50 - 17.84 Department: Housing and Residence Life Office Start Date: 10/28/2026 About this opportunity: Ball State University Housing and Residence Life is seeking an enthusiastic and collaborative team member to join our unit as an Accounting Specialist. This position supports the Assistant Director for Housing and Residence Life Fiscal Operations by assisting with the departmental activities of purchasing and credit card security and allocation, processing of payroll (professional, service, and student), monthly reporting, account analysis, and processing of transactions in the housing accounts receivable systems. This opportunity comes with a great benefits package that includes medical and prescription plans, dental, flexible spending and health savings accounts, paid time off, holiday pay, University-funded retirement, tuition discounts, and more! We invite you to apply today! Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the United States without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring: Position Function: Provide support to the Assistant Director for Housing and Residence Life Fiscal Operations by assisting with the departmental activities of purchasing and credit card security and allocation, processing of payroll (professional, service, and student), monthly reporting, account analysis, and processing of transactions in the housing accounts receivable systems. Duties & Responsibilities: 1. Provide support to the Assistant Director for Housing and Residence Life Fiscal Operations by assisting with the departmental activities of purchasing and credit card security and allocation, processing of payroll (professional, service, and student), monthly reporting, account analysis, and processing of transactions in the housing accounts receivable systems. 2. Assist with security and monitoring of the 30+ departmental credit cards; perform monthly reconciliation and on-line allocation of charges via the providers system; scan and upload all receipts, resolve violations with accounting; assist with training and answering questions. 3. Implement procedures prepared by supervisor and Payroll to process multiple payrolls correctly and on time using Kronos electronic time keeping system; process all Kronos Adjustment and Labor Distribution Forms: keep current on Payroll processing procedures, systems, and the union agreement as it relates to payroll and FMLA. 4. Input EPAFs for HRL student employees in a regular and timely manner including entering start dates in StarRez and using StarRez reports to process EPAFs terminating student positions. 5. Facilitate correct security access so managers can see their employees in Kronos. Coordinate and assist in Kronos training for new employees and supervisors. Serve as point person to answer questions and resolve issues related to payroll. Involves working with IT, Payroll, and all levels of employees and supervisors. 6. Enter Journal Vouchers in Banner, provide monthly account statements and balances to staff using ePrint, Banner, Banner SSB, and Argos. Analyze charges by activity code to prepare multiple spreadsheets. Assist with account reconciliations and analysis. 7. Process credit card refunds in CashNet, process charges and credits for Indiana Academy students and conferences via Banner Accounts Receivable. Assist Assistant Director in monitoring and entering credits and charges in StarRez. Answer questions regarding student accounts using StarRez and Banner Accounts Receivable. 8. Assist Assistant Director with Bike Locker and Microfridge rental programs. 9. Assist Assistant Director with asset audits and verifications, as well as various university policy training and compliance (cash handling, prizes, purchasing, etc.) . 10. Provide excellent customer service for the area of Housing and Residence Life, serve as back-up for other administrative support staff within the department. This includes being cross trained to perform a variety of roles and responsibilities as needed. 11. Perform other related duties as assigned. 12. Maintain regular and predictable attendance. Minimum Qualifications: Associate’s degree or equivalent combination of education and experience. Over one through three years of related experience. Preferred Qualifications: Prior experience working in a university setting, or with the Kronos payroll system, CashNet system, SciQuest, accounts receivable or accounting systems. How to apply: For inquiries, please contact: Associate Director of Fiscal Resources and Personnel at enewnam@bsu.edu Please follow upload instructions to attach all of the required supporting documents listed below.  Important: Do not use the Autofill feature when uploading your resume . Required Document: 1. Resume Optional Document (Recommended for Best Consideration): 2. Cover Letter detailing your qualifications for the position. What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer paid 10 to 24 vacation days, 12 sick days, and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. We do the same for you.  In fact, we'll cover 100 percent of the tuition costs for you to earn your undergraduate degree and 80 percent of your graduate tuition.  This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that show you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Staff (Exempt) and download our calculator spreadsheet."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Sports-Facilities-Supervisor_R-03404-1": {
      "title": "Sports Facilities Supervisor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Sports Facilities Supervisor Salary Grade: Exempt Staff 10 Compensation: $35,568.00 - 38,038.00 Department: Recreation Services_A Start Date: 10/28/2026 About this opportunity: The Ball State University Sports Facilities Department has an opportunity for a Sports Facilities Supervisor. This opportunity comes with competitive pay and a great benefit package that includes medical and prescription plans, dental, flexible spending and health savings accounts, paid time off, holiday pay, University-funded retirement, tuition discounts, and more! We are looking for an individual with a proven ability to supervise Field Facilities Attendants and student employees and ensure cleanliness, attractiveness, and timely set-ups of all athletic, recreation or physical education venues and special events, facilities, courts, or fields. The wage for this position will be $47,654.88. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the United States without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring: Position Function: Assign, monitor, direct, train, and evaluate work of Field Facilities Attendants and student employees to ensure cleanliness, attractiveness, and timely set-ups of all athletic, recreation or physical education venues and special events, facilities, courts, or fields. Duties & Responsibilities: 1. Plan, organize, assign, and review daily project work assignments of Field/Facilities Attendants and students. 2. Supervise, monitor, inspect, and coordinate daily operations, including special event set-ups and takedowns, ensuring methods, supplies, and equipment are properly utilized. 3. Assist with the proper allocation of Field Facilities Attendants for specific work assignments necessitated by emergency or special events. 4. Coordinate and inspect proper marking and set-ups of all athletic, recreation or physical education venues, courts, or fields according to established athletic and academic guidelines or standards. 5. Assist with the supervision and coordination of proper operations of Physical Education, Athletic and Recreation facilities and spaces. 6. Maintain records of employees, equipment, and supplies; includes attendance, overtime equalization charts, vacation schedules, performance records, disciplinary action reports, formal documentation, equipment and supplies evaluations, new product recommendations, and building maintenance/repair orders. 7. Orient and train staff, and make recommendations in all areas related to supervision, including but not limited to assisting with compensation, discipline, performance appraisals, training, and career development of Field Facilities Attendants and students. 8. Monitor and report personnel concerns, equipment and supply needs, and the need for maintenance and repair of physical facilities. 9. Monitor and enforce all safety, shop, and university rules and regulations and report problems to the Associate Director of Sports Facilities and Recreation and resolve problems appropriately. 10. Assist with the interviewing and hiring of employees and students as necessary. 11. Act as a liaison with various departments on campus with regard to general maintenance and operational issues. 12. Perform other related duties as assigned. 13. Maintain regular and predictable attendance. Minimum Qualifications: Eighteen months of training or education beyond high school or equivalent. Three through five years of experience in building services and grounds maintenance, including at least one year of first-line supervisory experience. Must possess and maintain a valid Indiana Driver’s License and be insurable under the university’s auto fleet policy. Preferred Qualifications: Associate’s degree. More than one year first-line supervisory experience. Experience working with bargaining unit employees. Experience working in a high school, university, or sports/recreation environment. Personal computer and software proficiency. How to apply: The wage for this position will be $47,654.88. For inquiries, please contact: BSU Sports Facilities Director of Sports, Recreation, and Concessions Building Services and Programs, Brandon L. Johnson: bljohnson@bsu.edu Please follow upload instructions to attach any supporting documents.    Important: Do not use the Autofill feature when uploading your resume. Required Document: 1. Resume Optional Document (Recommended for Best Consideration): 2. Cover Letter detailing your qualifications for the position. What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer paid 10 to 24 vacation days, 12 sick days, and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. We do the same for you.  In fact, we'll cover 100 percent of the tuition costs for you to earn your undergraduate degree and 80 percent of your graduate tuition.  This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that show you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Staff (Exempt) and download our calculator spreadsheet."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/University-Dining-Supervisor_R-03319": {
      "title": "University Dining Supervisor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: University Dining Supervisor Compensation: $43,888 Department: Woodworth Dining About this opportunity: Ball State University has a professional leadership opportunity available in University Dining that offers an excellent benefits package, paid time off and the opportunity for work/life balance. The University Dining Supervisor position is responsible for directing, overseeing, and leading all food and beverage operations within Ball State University Dining. This position is a day supervisor. The successful candidate will lead and direct subordinates resulting in good organization and minimal stress, promote teamwork, and execute excellent customer service that exceeds customer expectations. To learn more about Ball State University Dining, please visit our website at: http://www.bsu.edu/campuslife/dining This position supervises full-time and part-time food service workers, cashiers, custodians, group leaders and student employees. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring: Position Function: Under the direction of the General Manager, oversee and supervise employees in achieving excellence in customer satisfaction, food quality, service of food, employee efficiency and productivity, financial goals, and compliance with safety and sanitation standards, HACCP standards, Indiana Food Service Code regulations, and rules, policies and procedures of Ball State University: additional functions include but are not limited to food service forecasting and record keeping, physical inventory, subordinate training, food and supply purchasing, communication, executing promotions and advertisements, complying with branded concept license and franchise agreements and standards of operations, executing detailed plans and arrangements, contributing to menu, recipe, and concept development, and participating on a limited basis in preparation and serving of food or cashiering. Duties and Responsibilities: 1. Lead and supervise employees in executing correct, timely procedures in meeting license/franchise and department standards in relation to the preparation and service of all menu items, including but not limited to recipe preparation, food presentation, quality control, customer service, and sanitation and safety as defined by BSU manuals, handbooks, HACCP standards, Indiana Food Code, NRA ServSafe, and other industry standards; employ excellence in management techniques to exhibit evidence of teamwork and execution of excellent customer service that exceeds customer expectations in such areas, including but not limited to courtesy, speed of service, sense of urgency, product consistency, demonstrating a passion for excellence, utilizing fun and humor when appropriate, innovation and creativity, and other criteria. 2. Orient, coach, and train employees resulting in well-trained employees who consistently exhibit excellence in job knowledge and performance; ensure employees are well trained before working in any job assignment; provide accurate, balanced (positive and negative) feedback to employees regarding job performance and follow up on corrective measures; complete and maintain file documentation for all orientation, coaching, and training of each employee according to departmental procedures. 3. Count safe and audit safe record; audit cashier reports and submit thorough, accurate, cashier check-out reports to bookkeeper; properly report and account for shortages in safe or deposits of sales; complete documentation, report all unaccounted monies (over $20.00) immediately to the General Manager and/or University Police; check and approve all cashier refunds to customers and audit the no sale transactions of each cashier to prevent cashier theft; maintain accurate and up-to-date meal card system, including but not limited to reporting lost cards, verify account status, and overseeing the recording of off line transactions; administer university and departmental policies as they relate to money handling and reporting; ensure cashiers properly ring sales to record product movement and product value related to each brand upon which royalty payments to brand licensors or franchisors are based. 4. Utilize the Cbord Menu Management computer system to prepare menu item forecasts to (a) determine production of foods for service, and (b) correctly submit service statistics for historical data via computer record; under firm deadlines, scrutinize purchase requisitions and approve amounts of foods and supplies to be ordered based upon forecasted projections of sales and menu items, inventory levels, and other indicators; manage purchasing assignment with the utmost in business ethics and following policies and procedures of Ball State University; maintain appropriate inventory levels of foods and supplies as assigned, with neither being over or under-stocked; complete weekly inventory of foods and/or supplies with a high degree of accuracy. 5. Oversee and maintain adequate staffing following University procedures to schedule replacement employees; complete documentation related to scheduling regular and overtime staff; maintain correct telephone and address lists of all employees to facilitate this task; demonstrate a commitment to affirmative action and equal employment opportunity; communicate with peers and subordinates in a thorough, detailed, timely even-handed manner resulting in effective personal contact and/or the completion of management log entries that communicate necessary information to peers; attend shift meetings, unit and departmental management staff meetings, and relate telephone messages and/or other information accurately and in a timely manner; maintain confidentiality and ethical practices as relates to communications; in stressful situations, remain, calm, in control, and have a positive impact on others; manage disagreements effectively and create an environment where peers, employees, and customers are treated with dignity and respect and where rules, policies, and procedures are consistently administered. 6. Evaluate, investigate, and secure approval of General Manager and the Assistant Director of Personnel, or the Director, then issue warranted counseling or discipline to employees in a timely manner according to university policies and procedures; submit written documentation of all investigations, interviews, meetings, or conversations related to the situation in addition to copies of the properly issued disciplinary forms; accurately administer the union agreement and addenda thereto (including absence and tardiness policies and required record-keeping). 7. Unlock facility for the day’s operations and/or secure the facility for the periods of closure; observe safety and security precautions to prevent personal or employee injury, and theft of university or employee property; maintain personal and unit keys in a safe manner to prevent unauthorized use. 8. Establish, evaluate, and execute personal and unit goals, and contribute to departmental goal setting and achievement; serve in a contributory and effective manner on teams, committees, and task forces; demonstrate a professional appearance; wear clean, well-pressed clothing daily; follow prescribed dress code guidelines as outlined in departmental policies, rules, and regulations. 9. Evaluate employee performance and complete timely formal appraisal forms impartially and in an unbiased manner; submit draft appraisals for the approval of the General Manager; properly conduct the performance review meetings with employees; route completed forms in a timely manner. 10. Contribute to optimizing profitability through effective monitoring and supervision of food waste, portion control, inventory management, key control, theft and security controls, proper charging of sales to customers and employees by cashiers, and employees as they use and care for the facility, equipment, and furnishings; assist in evaluating food, labor, and other controllable costs; implement corrective measures as needed. 11. Collaborate in executing an effective marketing and promotion program for the unit in conjunction with the General Manager, approval from the Assistant Director of Personnel, and Assistant Director of Operations. 12. Provide planning of standard and custom menus, submit recipes for new menu items, and assist with development of sales mix for the unit; assist in planning and executing special events, catered events, and other non-routine food services. 13. Coordinate an effective laundry procedure to ensure proper supply of clean linen; maintain neat, accurate, require records; report maintenance and repair needs of building and equipment in a timely manner. 14. Perform food preparation, service and cashiering duties in emergency situations, and/or for short work periods to meet customer demand. 15. Perform other related duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: -Associates degree from an accredited institution or equivalent combination of education, credentials, certification, and experience. -At least one year of direct or related work experience (exclusive of teaching) in commercial or institutional food service, with demonstrated leadership and dynamic team building skills. -Skills in oral and written communication, strong analytical and problem-solving skills. Preferred Qualifications: -Bachelor's degree from an accredited institution. -Five years of direct or related work experience (exclusive of teaching) in commercial or institutional food service, with demonstrated leadership and dynamic team building skills supervisory experience. How to apply: For inquiries, please contact: University Dining at 765-285-1967. Supporting Documents Upload Instructions:  Please follow upload instructions to attach any supporting documents listed below. Important: Do not use the Autofill feature when uploading your resume. Required Document: 1. Resume Optional Document (Recommended for Best Consideration): 2. Cover Letter detailing your qualifications for the position. What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer paid 24 vacation days, 12 sick days and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. We do the same for you.  In fact, we'll cover 100 percent of the tuition costs for you to earn your undergraduate degree and 80 percent of your graduate tuition.  This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Professional and download the spreadsheet. If you are applying for a 10-month position or one with Burris or Indiana Academy, please select the corresponding calculator."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Instructor-of-Elementary-Education_R-01137": {
      "title": "Instructor of Elementary Education",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nPart time\n\nPosition Title:   Instructor of Elementary Education Compensation: $3,000 Department: Elementary Education - Temp Start Date: 04/29/2026 About this opportunity:   The Department of Elementary Education is seeking part-time semester contract faculty members to teach both undergraduate and graduate level courses, whose strengths and experiences are in the areas of curriculum and instruction. Positions are available Spring 2026. What you'll do and what you'll bring:   The Department of Elementary Education at Ball State University is seeking elementary education part-time semester contract faculty members to teach both undergraduate and graduate level courses, whose strengths and experiences are in the areas of curriculum and instruction. Position is available Spring 2026. Primary responsibilities for Master's degree candidates include teaching undergraduate courses in elementary and literacy education, with the expectation of teaching courses on-campus, partnering with school and community agencies, and performing other duties assigned by the department chairperson. Primary responsibilities for Doctorate degree candidates include teaching online graduate courses in elementary and literacy education. Minimum Qualifications: Masters or Doctorate in elementary education or related area from an accredited institution; at least three years elementary classroom teaching experience; knowledge of recent trends in elementary education. Authorization to work in the U.S. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. Preferred Qualifications: University teaching experience; knowledge of working with diverse learners; experience partnering with schools and community agencies; doctorate in elementary education or related area from an accredited institution. Applications will be held on file for one year from the posting date. How to apply:   Pre-Employment Screening: Requires successful completion of a background check and education verification, Information Regarding Transcripts: The option to upload transcripts is available. Original, official transcripts showing the highest related degree is required at the time of hire (even if obtained from BSU), Degree verification will be conducted. Please do not use the Autofill process from your resume. Required Documents: Resume Cover Letter In support of your application for this position, please prepare and submit a cover letter that describes how your qualifications and experience align with the elements of the position description (or leadership profile), in your cover letter, please select of our enduring values and describe how you have demonstrated a commitment to that value in your professional endeavors. Optional Documents: Letter of Recommendation Master's Transcripts Thank you for your interest in this position at Ball State University. Applications will be held on file for one year from the posting date. The screening and selection process is currently underway and will continue until successful candidates are chosen or the search is closed. Should a review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted using the contact information in your application. It is suggested that you bundle your documents together to ensure that you can include all required documents. Please contact Department Chairperson, Dr. Jackie Sydnor via email jtsydnor@bsu.edu  with questions."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Instructor-of-Early-Childhood--Youth--and-Family-Studies_R-03363": {
      "title": "Instructor of Early Childhood, Youth, and Family Studies",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nPart time\n\nPosition Title:   Instructor of Early Childhood, Youth, and Family Studies Compensation: $3000-$9000 Department: Early Chldhd Youth & Fam Studies - Temp Start Date: 01/04/2027 About this opportunity:   The Department of Early Childhood, Youth, and Family Studies at Ball State University seeks qualified part-time instructors to teach on-campus undergraduate courses in Family Science/ Human Development and Family Science. We are especially interested in candidates with academic or professional expertise in one or more of the following areas: Family Policy Family relationships and dynamics Parenting and parent education Family stress and resilience Work and family Adolescence and youth development Community and family services Research methods and grantwriting in the social sciences Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring:   Position Function : Adjunct instructors are responsible for providing high-quality, student-centered instruction; developing and maintaining course materials in Canvas; assessing student learning; communicating regularly with students; and collaborating with program faculty as needed. Courses are taught in person on Ball State University’s campus in Muncie, Indiana. Teaching assignments are based on departmental needs and the instructor’s qualifications and areas of expertise. Adjunct instructors may teach up to 3 courses (9 credit hours) per semester. Minimum qualifications: Master’s degree or higher in Family Science, Human Development and Family Science, Child Development, Psychology, Social Work, or a closely related field Academic preparation or professional experience relevant to the assigned course Ability to teach on campus during the scheduled course meeting times Strong communication and organizational skills Commitment to supporting the learning and success of undergraduate students   Preferred qualifications: Prior college-level teaching experience Experience using a learning-management system such as Canvas Relevant professional experience working with children, youth, adults, or families Certified Family Life Educator credential or eligibility for CFLE certification Ability to teach courses in more than one area of the Family Science or HDFS curriculum How to apply:   For inquiries, please contact: ecyfs@bsu.edu Please follow upload instructions to attach all of the required supporting documents listed below. *NOTE: Do not use the Autofill feature for resume. Cover Letter describing your teaching interests and area of expertise Resume/CV"
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Ball-State-Information-and-IT-OCC-Representative_R-03377": {
      "title": "Ball State Information and IT OCC Representative",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Ball State Information and IT OCC Representative Salary Grade: Staff 7 Compensation: $12.65 - 13.69 Department: Telephone Services Start Date: 11/09/2026 About this opportunity: If you enjoy being in the middle of the action and delight in mentoring students, this position might be for you. You’ll play a pivotal role in the Operations Control Center by supporting callers and responding to IT system outages, driving the coordinated resolution. You’ll also be monitoring BSU’s critical IT systems. Come join our team, apply today! Work Shift Schedule: Hours are as follows, with a $0.50 per hour second-shift premium: Monday - Friday, 3:00 pm – 11:30 pm. This role requires an on-campus presence; it is not a remote position. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the United States without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring: Position Function: Provide telephone assistance and general information to university offices, faculty, staff, students, and local, regional, national, and international callers. Operate  BSU radio communications. Monitor systems and respond to service impacting events supported by the Operations Control Center (OCC) by following standardized procedures. Serve as essential personnel as needed.   Duties & Responsibilities: 1. Provide prompt and courteous assistance and information to internal and external callers. This includes telephone numbers, special events and activities, building locations, directions, and emergency information. 2. Perform  ERP checks, server walk-thru, follow documented procedures to complete preventative system health checks. 3. Answer and direct incoming calls in an accurate, efficient, and profession manner, implementing exceptional customer service. 4. Assist callers with questions after the Helpdesk closes on weeknights and over weekends; reset passwords and complete Duo Mobile resets as needed. 5. Operate  BSU radio communication system for critical and non-critical situations. Relay work information to maintenance, University Police, custodial and housing personnel and maintain log of all radio calls. 6. Continually maintain a working knowledge of events occurring on BSU Campus and  BSU affiliated activities by using Ball State web pages, calendars, department contacts, news articles, as well as Marketing and Communication postings. 7. Respond to and take corrective action in response to system alarms and failures by determining technical priorities based on set standards and procedures. Analyze console messages; use problem/incident notifications and escalation procedures, and other documentation to resolve problems; contact and communicate job and/or system status with applicable System Service team members and support personnel. 8. Monitor and provide security for Operations Control Center and data centers. 9. Gather and analyze data to be used for training and staffing purposes. Train new, temporary, and student employees as needed. 10. Serve as essential personnel during severe weather or university crisis situations. 11. Assist Unified Communications technicians in testing lines and numbers during installations and repairs. 12. Perform other related duties as assigned. 13. Maintain regular and predictable attendance.   Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma or GED. Over three months through one year of customer service and IT related experience.   Preferred Qualifications: Eighteen months of education or training beyond high school. Over one year of related experience. Previous Ball State work experience. How to apply: For inquiries, contact Sharee Davis, Operations Control Center Manager, at the following email address: sbconatser@bsu.edu Please list three professional references within the online application. Supporting Documents Upload Instructions: Important:  Do not use the Autofill feature when uploading your resume. Please follow the upload instructions to attach the required supporting document listed below. Required Document: Resume Optional Document: Cover Letter What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer paid 10 to 24 vacation days, 12 sick days, and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. We do the same for you.  In fact, we'll cover 100 percent of the tuition costs for you to earn your undergraduate degree and 80 percent of your graduate tuition.  This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that show you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Staff (Exempt) and download our calculator spreadsheet."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Electrician-Supervisor_R-03382": {
      "title": "Electrician Supervisor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Electrician Supervisor Salary Grade: Exempt Staff 13A Compensation: $72,137.52 - 75,744.39 Department: Assoc VP Facilities Planning & Mgt_E Start Date: 10/07/2026 About this opportunity: Ball State University Facilities Planning and Management has an opportunity to work on the beautiful campus. This opportunity comes with excellent pay and a great benefits package that includes medical and prescription plans, dental, flexible spending and health savings accounts, paid time off, holiday pay, university-funded retirement, tuition discounts, and more. The ideal candidate will be flexible, and will possess great service skills with a willingness to learn. This is a full-time, on campus opportunity. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. HOURS 7:00 am to 3:30 pm Monday thru Friday Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the United States without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring: Position Function Supervise, schedule, and coordinate the activities of electrician personnel involved in related construction, renovation, maintenance, and repair projects to university buildings, equipment, and facilities to ensure compliance with established programs, standards, and procedures; assignments include responsibility for the electrician shop area. Duties & Responsibilities Supervise, schedule, and coordinate the activities of electrician skilled trades personnel in construction, renovation, maintenance, and repair projects to university buildings, equipment, and facilities to ensure compliance with established programs, standards, and procedures. Prepare cost estimates and material requisitions for projects and renovations; inspect work in process and completed work to ensure efficiency of operations and adherence to cost estimate. Assign and review work, orient and train staff, and make recommendations in all areas related to supervision, including, but not limited to, interviewing and selection, discipline, performance appraisal, and training and career development of personnel. Monitor and enforce all safety, shop, and university rules and regulations and report problems to the Assistant Manager of Building Operations and resolve problems appropriately. Coordinate with stakeholders to determine project requirements; maintain liaison with all parties involved to discuss any modifications and facilitate the resolution of project problems; review and recommend changes and modifications to blueprints and/or job specifications as appropriate. Monitor work order to completion of project/work to ensure that labor, supplies, and materials are charged to the appropriate work order; add change orders to original work order when additional work is requested and approved. Update, maintain, and train workers on various job-related chemicals, environmental and safety concerns, and SDS/OSHA regulations; maintain a working knowledge and awareness of all Environmental Health and Safety programs. Plan, develop, write, and implement various preventative maintenance programs when appropriate; set up programs using a work order system and monitor for conformance; monitor reports generated from system regarding backlog of work, repeat work, etc.; propose changes in assignment and staffing as necessary. Prepare reports, setting forth analyses, progress, adverse trends, and appropriate recommendations and/or conclusions regarding maintenance and construction projects; use personal computer to generate reports and analysis with spreadsheet, word processing, and work order software. Perform other related duties as assigned. Maintain regular and predictable attendance. All of the above essential functions require varying degrees of independence, judgment, and discretion. Requires the ability to efficiently operate a computer keyboard and programs. Minimum Qualifications Associate’s degree or equivalent Over five years of experience in the electrician trade and at least three years of supervisory experience Must hold a valid Indiana Driver's License and be insurable under the university's auto fleet policy; personal computer and software proficiency. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution Completion of an apprenticeship program Over three years supervisory experience. How to apply: For inquiries, please contact: Kevin Ward, Manager of Building Operations, 765-285-5090, ksward@bsu.edu Important:  Do not use the Autofill feature when uploading your resume. Resume - Required Cover Letter detailing your qualifications for the position - Optional What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer paid 10 to 24 vacation days, 12 sick days, and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. We do the same for you.  In fact, we'll cover 100 percent of the tuition costs for you to earn your undergraduate degree and 80 percent of your graduate tuition.  This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that show you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Staff (Exempt) and download our calculator spreadsheet."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Plumbing-and-Welding-Supervisor_R-03391": {
      "title": "Plumbing and Welding Supervisor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Plumbing and Welding Supervisor Salary Grade: Exempt Staff 13A Compensation: $72,137.52 - 75,744.39 Department: Assoc VP Facilities Planning & Mgt_P (Chris Sizelove Start Date: 10/08/2026 About this opportunity: Ball State University Facilities Planning and Management has an opportunity to work on the beautiful campus. This opportunity comes with excellent pay and a great benefits package that includes medical and prescription plans, dental, flexible spending and health savings accounts, paid time off, holiday pay, university-funded retirement, tuition discounts, and more. The ideal candidate will be flexible, and will possess great service skills with a willingness to learn. This is a full-time, on campus opportunity. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. HOURS 7:00 am to 3:30 pm Monday thru Friday Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the United States without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring: Position Function: Supervise, schedule, and coordinate the activities of plumbers and welders involved in construction, renovation, maintenance, and repair projects to university buildings, equipment, and facilities to ensure compliance with established programs, standards, and procedures. Duties & Responsibilities: 1. Supervise, schedule, and coordinate the activities of plumbers and welders in construction, renovation, maintenance, and repair projects to university buildings, equipment, and facilities to ensure compliance with established programs, standards, and procedures. 2. Prepare cost estimates and material requisitions for projects and renovations; inspect work in process and completed work to ensure efficiency of operations and adherence to cost estimate. 3. Assign and review work, orient and train staff, and make recommendations in all areas related to supervision, including, but not limited, to interviewing and selection, compensation, discipline, performance appraisal, and training and career development of personnel. 4. Monitor and enforce all safety, shop, and university rules and regulations and report problems to the Superintendent of Building Maintenance and resolve problems appropriately. 5. Coordinate with users and/or departments to determine project requirements; maintain liaison with all parties involved to discuss any modifications and facilitate the resolution of project problems; review and recommend changes and modifications to blueprints and/or job specifications as appropriate. 6. Monitor work order to completion of project/work to ensure that labor, supplies, and materials are charged to the appropriate work order; add change orders to original work order when additional work is requested and approved. 7. Update, maintain, and train workers on various job-related chemicals, environmental and safety concerns, and MSDS/OSHA regulations; maintain a working knowledge and awareness of all Environmental Health and Safety programs. 8. Plan, develop, write, and implement various preventative maintenance programs when appropriate; set up programs using a work order system and monitor for conformance; monitor reports generated from system regarding backlog of work, repeat work, etc.; propose changes in assignment and staffing as necessary. 9. Prepare reports, setting forth analyses, progress, adverse trends, and appropriate recommendations and/or conclusions regarding maintenance and construction projects; use personal computer to generate reports and analysis with spreadsheet, word processing, and work order software. 10. Perform other related duties as assigned. 11. Maintain regular and predictable attendance. Minimum Qualifications: Associate’s degree or equivalent. Over five years of experience in the appropriate trade and at least three years of supervisory experience. Must possess and maintain a valid Indiana Driver’s License and be insurable under the university’s auto fleet policy. Personal computer and software proficiency. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree. Completion of an apprenticeship program. Proficiency in at least one area or discipline. Over three years supervisory experience. How to apply: For inquiries, please contact:  Kevin Ward, Manager of Building Operations at 765-285-5090 or ksward@bsu.edu Important:  Do not use the Autofill feature when uploading your resume. Cover Letter detailing your qualifications for the position - Optional Resume - Required What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer paid 10 to 24 vacation days, 12 sick days, and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. We do the same for you.  In fact, we'll cover 100 percent of the tuition costs for you to earn your undergraduate degree and 80 percent of your graduate tuition.  This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that show you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Staff (Exempt) and download our calculator spreadsheet."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Entrepreneurship-Center-Director_R-03285-1": {
      "title": "Entrepreneurship Center Director",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Entrepreneurship Center Director Compensation: $100,000 - $170,000 Department: Management About this opportunity: The Department of Management at Ball State University’s Miller College of Business invites applications from accomplished professionals to lead the entrepreneurship program in the Miller College of Business, with a start as early as January, and as late as July 2027. This is an excellent opportunity for a committed entrepreneurship professional who enjoys working in a collaborative environment to foster student, academic, business, and community programs and partnerships, and wants to contribute to regional economic growth. This exciting opportunity will shape the future of entrepreneurship in the Miller College while driving impactful collaboration between academia and business. We seek a dynamic, forward-thinking leader who will bring industry expertise, a strong network of professional connections, a proven ability to develop innovative curricula and build academic programs, and a commitment to building industry and community partnerships. The Center Director will be an integral member of the Department of Management, entrusted with driving the mission, strategic growth, and operational excellence of the entrepreneurship programs in the Miller College of Business. This is a full-time, on-site position based at Ball State University in Muncie, Indiana. Appropriately qualified candidates will be considered for tenure and academic rank in the Department of Management. Candidates with a PhD in a related field will be considered for appointment as a tenure track faculty based on the quality of their research, current academic rank, and teaching experience. Range for non-tenure track appointment: $100,000 - $120,000 Range for tenure-track appointment: $150,000 - $170,000 Candidates must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring: Position Function: The Entrepreneurship Center Director will provide vision and leadership to the entrepreneurship programs; define the strategic direction and goals; develop curriculum; build enrollment and engage with students; develop and nurture industry and community contacts; cultivate a strong advisory board; network with alumni; and encourage internships and experiential learning opportunities. The position also serves as the central point of coordination for program logistics, communications, and day-to-day operations on matters concerning entrepreneurship in the Miller College. This is an important leadership role, as it connects with several academic units on campus, collaborates with Ball State University’s Center for Innovation and Collaboration, and requires engagement with students, affiliated faculty, entrepreneurs, and the community. Salary Range:   $100,000 - $120,000 $150,000 - $170,000 (for faculty appointment with tenure)    Duties and Responsibilities:   1 . Serve as Center Director responsible for strategic direction and operational excellence, and as a focal point for coordination of the entrepreneurial programs in the college. 2. Teach up to nine credit hours each fall and spring semester in entrepreneurship, leadership, or related courses (commensurate with tenure and rank), at the undergraduate or graduate level, which may be delivered on campus or online, synchronously or asynchronously, depending on expertise and the department’s needs. 3. Promote the entrepreneurship major and minor to prospective students, mentor students, encourage internships and experiential learning opportunities, and help students develop their business plans. 4. Expand and sustain the Entrepreneurship advisory board and organize and lead meetings and events to advance fundraising and promotion of the entrepreneurship program. 5. Partner with the Ball State University Foundation development team to develop relationships with potential donors and raise funds to support an array of Entrepreneurship Center activities. 6. Encourage student participation in competitions and conferences; and sustain and enrich the program’s guest speaker series. 7. Collaborate with department faculty in reviewing the entrepreneurship curriculum and developing new content based on the program's current and evolving needs. 8. Conduct scholarly research (commensurate with tenure and rank), primarily in entrepreneurship, leadership, strategy, or related areas, and publish in high-quality academic journals. 9. Provide service to the university, engage with the business and academic community, address the role of business as a force for good in society, and generally support regional economic development. 10. Attend department and college meetings and serve on department and college committees. 11. Perform other related duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Earned Master’s degree from an AACSB-accredited institution in Entrepreneurship, Strategic Management, Business Administration, or other relevant field. Five years of experience with academia, business or entrepreneurial organizations, or related areas. For appointment as tenured faculty - PhD in Entrepreneurship, Strategic Management, Business Administration or a closely related field from an AACSB-accredited institution.   Preferred Qualifications: A network of industry contacts, experience in content or curriculum development and delivery, and a track record of building academic programs and/or business partnerships. Evidence of career advancement in business or entrepreneurial organizations, or evidence of scholarship in a business-related field. For appointment as tenured faculty - A record of scholarly research (commensurate with tenure and rank), primarily in entrepreneurship, leadership, strategy, or related areas, with publications in high-quality academic journals. How to apply: For inquiries about the opportunity, please contact: Dr. Abhishek Srivastava. abhishek.srivastava@bsu.edu   Important: Please follow upload instructions for attaching all required documents listed below. Only complete applications will be considered. REQUIRED APPLICATION DOCUMENTS: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Within the application, please provide names and contact information for three (3) professional references. APPLICATION DEADLINE: This position will remain open until filled with a consideration date of November 16, 2026, 12:01 a.m. Candidates submitting application materials on or before this date will receive full consideration. Review of applications will continue until the position is filled. What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer paid 24 vacation days, 12 sick days and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. We do the same for you.  In fact, we'll cover 100 percent of the tuition costs for you to earn your undergraduate degree and 80 percent of your graduate tuition.  This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Professional and download the spreadsheet. If you are applying for a 10-month position or one with Burris or Indiana Academy, please select the corresponding calculator."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Business-Operations-Analyst_R-03415": {
      "title": "Business Operations Analyst",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Business Operations Analyst Compensation: $60,000 - $71,000 Department: VP for Information Technology_B About this opportunity: The Business Operations Analyst is a key professional role within Information Technology, providing advanced financial, operational, and systems analysis to support the University’s technology operations. This position manages and analyzes critical functions including budgeting, procurement, enterprise billing, HR position management, vendor and contract administration, and financial reporting. The analyst also develops automated reconciliation models, dashboards, and process improvements that reduce manual effort, strengthen internal controls, improve data accuracy, and provide greater transparency for decision-making. Working collaboratively with IT, Finance, HR, Procurement, and other campus partners, this position requires strong analytical skills, independent judgment, technical proficiency, and the ability to manage complex financial and operational processes. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring: Position Function: The IT Business Operations Analyst provides advanced operational, financial, and systems analysis support for Information Technology. This position integrates financial management, enterprise billing systems, procurement processes, HR position management, vendor coordination, and data analytics to improve operational efficiency through automation and process optimization. The analyst focuses on improving IT business processes, supporting budgeting and resource management, and advancing transparency and accountability across IT services. These duties require advanced independent judgment, analytical expertise, and technical proficiency across enterprise financial and workflow systems, as well as the ability to manage high-volume transactional data while ensuring compliance, accuracy, and operational efficiency.  Duties & Responsibilities 1. Manage procurement lifecycle activities, including preparation of purchase requisitions and purchase orders, invoice validation, vendor communication, credit card reconciliation, receipt verification, and payment processing in compliance with university policy.  2. Prepare, validate, and process Banner journal vouchers, accounting feeds, budget transfers, and financial adjustments; reconcile FOAPAL activity and resolve discrepancies in coordination with the Controller’s Office.  3. Process and audit HR position actions, including position modifications, postings, hiring proposals, and changes related to IT personnel; coordinate with HR/Payroll to ensure timely and accurate processing.  4. Administer and reconcile monthly enterprise billing processes, including voice, network, server, print management, cloud services, and digital platforms; ensure accuracy of accounting feeds before Banner upload.  5. Develop and maintain automated reconciliation models, dashboards, and financial reporting tools to improve operational transparency and decision-making efficiency.  6. Support month-end and year-end close processes, including billing audits, recharge balancing, accounting feed verification, and preparation of supporting documentation for grants and foundation reporting.  7. Provide analytical support for server, cloud (e.g., Azure), and infrastructure cost recovery models; support recharge methodology development and automation enhancements.  8. Respond to departmental inquiries regarding billing, recharge calculations, budget activity, and procurement processes; provide documentation and reporting as requested.  9. Identify, recommend, and implement workflow automation and process improvements to reduce manual effort, strengthen internal controls, and enhance data integrity across enterprise systems.  10.  Collaborate cross-functionally with Unified Communications, Unified Technology Support, Procurement, HR, and Business Affairs to coordinate financial operations and system integrations.  11.  Support the Executive Director for Enterprise Technology Project Management and IT Budgets with special projects, financial modeling, audits, and operational analyses as assigned.  12.  Maintain and monitor contract lifecycle documentation within ServiceNow and procurement systems; track renewals, expiration dates, purchase order status, and vendor compliance requirements.  13.  Administer and audit cellular device allowances and electronic device stipends; maintain fiscal year tracking records and ensure compliance with institutional policy.  14. Perform other related duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in accounting or a related financial field. Skills in using Microsoft Excel. Or, instead of a Bachelor’s degree: an Associate’s degree plus an additional combination of education or​ accounting/finance experience equivalent to two years. Three years of experience in business or financial management.  At least one year of experience with Banner Finance and Jaggaer (Procurement).  Excellent communication skills. Preferred Qualifications: Advanced degree in accounting or a related financial field. Experience in university financial management, planning, and/or administration. Three years of experience with Banner Finance and Jaggaer (Procurement). How to apply: For inquiries, please contact:  Mark Watters, Executive Director for Enterprise Technology Project Management and IT Budgets, at the following email address:  mwatters@bsu.edu Please list three professional references within the online application. Supporting Documents Upload Instructions: Important:   Do not use the Autofill feature when uploading your resume. Please follow the upload instructions to attach all required supporting documents listed below. Required Document: Resume Optional Document: Cover Letter What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer paid 24 vacation days, 12 sick days and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. We do the same for you.  In fact, we'll cover 100 percent of the tuition costs for you to earn your undergraduate degree and 80 percent of your graduate tuition.  This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Professional and download the spreadsheet. If you are applying for a 10-month position or one with Burris or Indiana Academy, please select the corresponding calculator."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Administration-Building-Security-Officer_R-03410": {
      "title": "Administration Building Security Officer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-09\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Administration Building Security Officer Salary Grade: Staff 10A Compensation: $19.20 - 20.75 Department: Public Safety Start Date: 11/09/2026 About this opportunity: Ball State University is inviting applications for the position of Administration Building Security Officer to champion the safety, security, and operational integrity of our campus community. This non-sworn, non-law enforcement position is responsible for maintaining a safe, secure, and highly service-oriented environment within the facility. The ideal candidate will excel at building positive relationships across campus, delivering top-tier customer service, and supporting a safe, high-integrity environment for our students, faculty, and staff. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the United States without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring: Position Function: The Administration Building Security Officer is responsible for supporting a safe, secure, and service-oriented environment within the facility. This position performs routine security functions including monitoring building access, conducting patrols of the building, observing and reporting safety concerns, assisting visitors, and responding to non-emergency incidents. This is a non-sworn, non-law enforcement position and does not include arrest authority. The Security Officer is expected to interact professionally with students, faculty, staff, and visitors while supporting the university’s commitment to safety, customer service, and operational excellence. Duties and Responsibilities: Security Operations 1. Monitor and patrol the Administration Building and surrounding areas to ensure the safety and security of university property and occupants. 2. Conduct routine interior and exterior patrols on foot as assigned. 3. Unlock and secure facilities according to established schedules and procedures. 4. Monitor entrances and exits to prevent unauthorized access. 5. Observe and report suspicious activity, security concerns, safety hazards, and policy violations. Access Control & Monitoring 6. Verify identification and credentials of employees, visitors, contractors, and vendors to the Office of the President. 7. Monitor Administration Building security cameras. 8. Respond appropriately to building alarms and access issues. 9. Adhere to key control and access card procedures in accordance with university policy. Customer Service & Assistance 10. Provide information, directions, and assistance to students, employees, and visitors. 11. Serve as a visible and approachable presence within the Administration Building. 12. Promote a welcoming and professional campus environment. 13. Respond courteously and effectively to routine requests and concerns. Incident Response & Reporting 14. Respond to non-emergency and certain emergency incidents and provide appropriate assistance. 15. Contact campus police when necessary. 16. Prepare accurate, timely, and detailed incident and activity reports. 17. Document security concerns, accidents, injuries, and unusual occurrences. Emergency Preparedness 18. Assist with emergency response procedures including evacuations, shelter-in-place operations, and building lockdowns. 19. Support university emergency management efforts during incidents or severe weather events. 20. Participate in required safety and emergency preparedness training. Collaboration 21. Work collaboratively with campus police, emergency management, facilities personnel, administrators, and other university departments. 22. Assist with security support for meetings, special events, and after-hours operations as assigned. 23. Perform other related duties as assigned. 24. Maintain regular and predictable attendance. Minimum Qualifications At least 18 months of education beyond high school or equivalent. One (1) year of experience in security, safety, customer service, facilities operations, or a related field. Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively both verbally and in writing. Ability to exercise sound judgment and maintain professionalism in a variety of situations. Basic computer and technology skills. Must pass a polygraph test pre-offer. Strong observational and problem-solving skills. Ability to maintain confidentiality and handle sensitive situations appropriately. Strong interpersonal and customer service skills. Ability to remain calm and effective during stressful or emergency situations. Preferred Qualifications Experience working in higher education, healthcare, government, or institutional security settings. Experience using video security systems, access control systems, or incident reporting software. Training in de-escalation techniques, conflict resolution, or emergency response. How to apply: Please apply via the online Ball State University job portal . Please list three professional references within the online application. Supporting Documents Upload Instructions: Important:  Do  not  use the Autofill feature when uploading your resume. Required Document: Resume Optional Document: Cover Letter   detailing your qualifications for the position. What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer paid 10 to 24 vacation days, 12 sick days, and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. We do the same for you.  In fact, we'll cover 100 percent of the tuition costs for you to earn your undergraduate degree and 80 percent of your graduate tuition.  This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that show you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Staff (Exempt) and download our calculator spreadsheet."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/HVAC-R-Technician_R-03301-1": {
      "title": "HVAC-R Technician",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-09\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: HVAC-R Technician Compensation: $37.50 - $37.50 Department: District Energy Station North (Tyler Ferrell Start Date: 09/25/2026 About this opportunity: Ball State University Facilities Planning and Management has an opportunity to work on the beautiful campus. This opportunity comes with excellent pay and a great benefits package that includes medical and prescription plans, dental, flexible spending and health savings accounts, paid time off, holiday pay, university-funded retirement, tuition discounts, and more. The ideal candidate will be flexible, and will possess great service skills with a willingness to learn. This is a full-time, on campus opportunity. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. HOURS 2nd Shift: 3:30 p.m. to 12:00 midnight Monday through Friday What you'll do and what you'll bring: Position Function Under supervision, perform service required in the installation, operation, maintenance, and repair of heating, ventilating, air conditioning, and refrigeration equipment and related equipment, complying with EPA, OSHA, and all appropriate regulations and codes. Water treatment and water cleaning duties are excluded from this classification. Duties & Responsibilities 1. Perform maintenance and repair work on heating, ventilating, air conditioning, and refrigeration equipment, and report work performed on Preventive Maintenance Forms. Requires the physical ability to climb, balance, kneel, crouch, crawl, reach, walk, push, pull, lift, finger, grasp, feel, talk, hear, stand and/or stoop for long periods of time, and exert in excess of 100 pounds of force occasionally, 50 pounds of force frequently, and 20 pounds of force constantly. Task requires the visual ability to distinguish color and perceive depth. Task requires the ability to operate various hand and power tools, ladders, scaffolds, and measuring instrumentation and equipment. Employee is exposed to inside and outside environmental conditions, extreme heat and cold, high humidity, noise, heights, fumes, odors, oils, chemicals, dust, and may be required to wear a filter mask, respirator, and various protective clothing and/or equipment. Task requires the mental ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information. 2. Install, adjust, and repair refrigeration, heating, air conditioning, and ventilating systems, including but not limited to ice machines, freezers, refrigerators, drinking fountains, and other appliances. Requires the physical ability to climb, balance, kneel, crouch, crawl, reach, walk, push, pull, lift, finger, grasp, feel, talk, hear, stand and/or stoop for long periods of time, and exert in excess of 100 pounds of force occasionally, 50 pounds of force frequently, and 20 pounds of force constantly. Task requires the visual ability to distinguish color and perceive depth. Task requires the ability to operate various hand and power tools, ladders, scaffolds, and measuring instrumentation and equipment. Employee is exposed to inside and outside environmental conditions, extreme heat and cold, high humidity, noise, heights, fumes, odors, oils, chemicals, dust, and may be required to wear a filter mask, respirator, and various protective clothing and/or equipment. Task requires the mental ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information. 3. Troubleshoot, adjust, repair, and calibrate controls on all HVAC/R equipment. Read and monitor gauges, meters, and thermostats, and adjust and repair control systems. Requires the physical ability to climb, balance, kneel, crouch, crawl, reach, walk, push, pull, lift, finger, grasp, feel, talk, hear, stand and/or stoop for long periods of time, and exert up to 100 pounds of force occasionally, up to 50 pounds of force frequently, and up to 20 pounds of force constantly. Task requires the visual ability to distinguish color and perceive depth. Task requires the ability to operate various hand and power tools, ladders, scaffolds, and measuring instrumentation and equipment. Employee is exposed to inside and outside environmental conditions, extreme heat and cold, high humidity, noise, heights, fumes, odors, oils, chemicals, dust, and may be required to wear a filter mask, respirator, and various protective clothing and/or equipment. Task requires the mental ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information . 4. Inspect, maintain, and lubricate HVAC/R related pumps, motors, dampers, and other related equipment; inspect and clean coils and fans; inspect belts, vibration absorbers, and other related equipment. Requires the physical ability to climb, balance, kneel, crouch, crawl, reach, walk, push, pull, lift, finger, grasp, feel, talk, hear, stand and/or stoop for long periods of time, and exert up to 100 pounds of force occasionally, up to 50 pounds of force frequently, and up to 20 pounds of force constantly. Task requires the visual ability to distinguish color and perceive depth. Task requires the ability to operate various hand and power tools, ladders, scaffolds, and measuring instrumentation and equipment. Employee is exposed to inside and outside environmental conditions, extreme heat and cold, high humidity, noise, heights, fumes, odors, oils, chemicals, dust, and may be required to wear a filter mask, respirator, and various protective clothing and/or equipment. Task requires the mental ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information. 5. Maintain and operate central chilling plant equipment, geothermal heat pump chillers, fluid coolers, cooling towers, and the chilled and hot water distribution system, including large tonnage centrifugal chillers, heat pump chillers, air dirt separators, distribution pumps, and associated control systems. Requires the physical ability to climb, balance, kneel, crouch, crawl, reach, walk, push, pull, lift, finger, grasp, feel, talk, hear, stand and/or stoop for long periods of time, and exert in excess of 100 pounds of force occasionally, 50 pounds of force frequently, and 20 pounds of force constantly. Task requires the visual ability to distinguish color and perceive depth. Task requires the ability to operate various hand and power tools, ladders, scaffolds, and measuring instrumentation and equipment. Employee is exposed to inside and outside environmental conditions, extreme heat and cold, high humidity, noise, heights, fumes, odors, oils, chemicals, dust, and may be required to wear a filter mask, respirator, and various protective clothing and/or equipment. Task requires the mental ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information. 6. Perform preventive maintenance and repair on swimming pool and fountain mechanical equipment, including pumps, motors, heaters, heat exchangers, filters, valves, and related equipment. Water treatment, water chemistry, chemical dosing, bacteriological testing, and water or basin cleaning for pools, fountains, and other water features are excluded from this classification. Requires the physical ability to climb, balance, kneel, crouch, crawl, reach, walk, push, pull, lift, finger, grasp, feel, talk, hear, stand and/or stoop for long periods of time, and exert in excess of 100 pounds of force occasionally, 50 pounds of force frequently, and 20 pounds of force constantly. Task requires the visual ability to distinguish color and perceive depth. Task requires the ability to operate various hand and power tools, ladders, scaffolds, and measuring instrumentation and equipment. Employee is exposed to inside and outside environmental conditions, extreme heat and cold, high humidity, noise, heights, fumes, odors, oils, chemicals, dust, and may be required to wear a filter mask, respirator, and various protective clothing and/or equipment. Task requires the mental ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information . 7. Read and interpret drawings, diagrams, and specifications pertaining to heating, ventilation, air conditioning, and refrigeration equipment to ensure compliance with appropriate codes. Requires the physical ability to kneel, reach, stand, walk, finger, grasp, talk, hear, and exert up to 10 pounds of force occasionally. Task requires the visual ability to distinguish color and perceive depth. Task requires the ability to efficiently operate a computer keyboard as prescribed by management. Employee is exposed to inside environmental conditions. Task requires the mental ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information . 8. Acquire and maintain knowledge of various job-related chemicals, environmental concerns, and technological improvements and advancements, including refrigerant transition requirements for low global warming potential refrigerants. Requires the physical ability to finger, grasp, stand, and exert up to 10 pounds of force occasionally. Task requires the visual ability to distinguish color, read small print, and perceive depth. Employee is exposed to inside and outside environmental conditions. Task requires the mental ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information . 9. Inspect, maintain, repair, and install insulation on water lines, steam lines, pumps, and other HVAC/R related equipment. Work on steam systems under this position is limited to low pressure systems operating at or below 15 pounds per square inch. High pressure steam generation and distribution remain the responsibility of the Heat Plant and District Energy Station classifications. Requires the physical ability to climb, balance, kneel, crouch, crawl, reach, walk, push, pull, lift, finger, grasp, feel, hear, stand and/or stoop for extended periods of time, and exert in excess of 10 pounds of force constantly. Task requires the visual ability to distinguish color and perceive depth. Task requires the ability to operate various hand and power tools, ladders, scaffolds, and measuring instrumentation and equipment. Employee is exposed to inside and outside environmental conditions, extreme heat and cold, high humidity, noise, heights, fumes, odors, oils, chemicals, dust, and may be required to wear a filter mask, respirator, and various protective clothing and/or equipment. Task requires the mental ability to receive, follow, and provide oral instructions and information, and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information . 10. Operate building automation systems related to HVAC/R, including computer hardware and software. Requires the ability to efficiently operate a computer keyboard as prescribed by management. Task requires the physical ability to climb, balance, kneel, crouch, crawl, reach, walk, push, pull, lift, finger, grasp, feel, hear, stand and/or stoop for extended periods of time, and exert in excess of 10 pounds of force constantly. Task requires the visual ability to distinguish color and perceive depth. Task requires the ability to operate various hand and power tools, measuring instrumentation and equipment. Employee is exposed to inside environmental conditions, extreme heat and cold, high humidity, noise, and heights. Task requires the mental ability to receive, follow, and provide oral instructions and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information. 11. Construct, fabricate, remodel, maintain, and repair air system fabrications for HVAC/R systems as directed. Requires the physical ability to climb, balance, kneel, crouch, crawl, reach, walk, push, pull, lift, finger, grasp, feel, talk, hear, stand and/or stoop for long periods of time, and exert in excess of 100 pounds of force occasionally, 50 pounds of force frequently, and 20 pounds of force constantly. Task requires the visual ability to distinguish color and perceive depth. Task requires the ability to operate high pressure water hoses, various hand and power tools, ladders, and measuring instrumentation and equipment. Employee is exposed to inside and outside environmental conditions, extreme heat and cold, high humidity, noise, heights, fumes, odors, oils, chemicals, dust, and may be required to wear a filter mask, respirator, and various protective clothing and/or equipment. Task requires the mental ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information. 12. Maintain accurate records of work orders, material usage, and refrigerant purchase, use, recovery, and disposal in compliance with EPA recordkeeping requirements under Section 608 of the Clean Air Act and applicable HFC regulations. Requires the physical ability to kneel, reach, stand, walk, finger, grasp, talk, hear, and exert up to 10 pounds of force occasionally. Task requires the visual ability to distinguish color and perceive depth. Task requires the ability to efficiently operate a computer keyboard as prescribed by management. Employee is exposed to inside environmental conditions. Task requires the mental ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information . 13. Perform other duties as assigned. May require any or all of the above-mentioned abilities . Minimum Qualifications 1. High School diploma or equivalent (GED). 2. Successful completion of a US Department of Labor registered apprenticeship program in Heating, Ventilation and Air Conditioning; or five (5) years of commercial HVAC or refrigeration experience, including experience with low pressure chillers; or an equivalent combination of education and experience from which comparable job knowledge can be acquired as determined by Ball State University. 3. EPA Section 608 Universal certification as noted in federal register 40 CFR 82 Sub Part F to handle all refrigerants. Proof of certification type must be provided upon request. Universal certification is required because this position services equipment in both high pressure (Type II) and low pressure (Type III) categories, including chillers. 4. Must be able to read and comprehend all specified policies and procedures for safety, hazardous materials information, University policies, procedures, and communications, and perform mathematical functions. 5. Scissor lift operator certification in accordance with OSHA and ANSI standards, or the ability to obtain certification within ninety (90) days of hire. 6. Must possess and maintain a valid Drivers License and be insurable under the university's auto fleet policy. 7. Must be able to perform all mental and physical requirements as outlined in each job duty. 8. Must be 18 years or older. Preferred Qualifications 1. Vocational School Training. 2. Experience with electronic controls for HVAC systems. 3. Over six (6) years HVAC/R experience. 4. Experience with centrifugal chillers with over 1000 tons in capacity. 5. Experience with geothermal heat pump and ground source district energy systems. 6. HVAC journey worker certification through a US Department of Labor registered apprenticeship program. 7. R-410A safety training and training in the safe handling of A2L (mildly flammable) refrigerants. 8. OSHA 10 or OSHA 30 certification. 9. Electrical systems experience. How to apply: For inquiries, please contact: Tyler Ferrell, HVAC-R Supervisor at 765-285-3270 or taferrell@bsu.edu Important:  Do not use the Autofill feature when uploading your resume. Optional documents (Recommended for best consideration). Resume Cover Letter detailing your qualifications for the position. Must provide all minimum qualifications through attachments and/or completing application to be considered. What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer a generous paid time off program and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust short-term disability, long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. We do the same for you.  In fact, we'll cover 100 percent of the tuition costs for you to earn your undergraduate degree and 80 percent of your graduate tuition. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow.   Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Service and download our calculator spreadsheet."
    },
