nd to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information . 13. Perform other duties as assigned. May require any or all of the above-mentioned abilities . Minimum Qualifications 1. High School diploma or equivalent (GED). 2. Successful completion of a US Department of Labor registered apprenticeship program in Heating, Ventilation and Air Conditioning; or five (5) years of commercial HVAC or refrigeration experience, including experience with low pressure chillers; or an equivalent combination of education and experience from which comparable job knowledge can be acquired as determined by Ball State University. 3. EPA Section 608 Universal certification as noted in federal register 40 CFR 82 Sub Part F to handle all refrigerants. Proof of certification type must be provided upon request. Universal certification is required because this position services equipment in both high pressure (Type II) and low pressure (Type III) categories, including chillers. 4. Must be able to read and comprehend all specified policies and procedures for safety, hazardous materials information, University policies, procedures, and communications, and perform mathematical functions. 5. Scissor lift operator certification in accordance with OSHA and ANSI standards, or the ability to obtain certification within ninety (90) days of hire. 6. Must possess and maintain a valid Drivers License and be insurable under the university's auto fleet policy. 7. Must be able to perform all mental and physical requirements as outlined in each job duty. 8. Must be 18 years or older. Preferred Qualifications 1. Vocational School Training. 2. Experience with electronic controls for HVAC systems. 3. Over six (6) years HVAC/R experience. 4. Experience with centrifugal chillers with over 1000 tons in capacity. 5. Experience with geothermal heat pump and ground source district energy systems. 6. HVAC journey worker certification through a US Department of Labor registered apprenticeship 